WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:03.206
(inquisitive music)

00:00:06.689 --> 00:00:11.689
(upbeat music)
(John sighs and claps)

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:16.470
- The Middle East, the part
of Asia that Europeans see

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:20.253
as the middle of what
they see as the east.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.730
Sort of arbitrary. Whatever,
we call it the Middle East.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:24.930
This part of the world

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.020
is literally where civilization started,

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.480
right here, in modern-day Iraq.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.410
And over the years,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:34.140
the borders here have
been redrawn many times

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.410
as empires have ebbed and
flowed through this region.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.720
By the way, I didn't make this time lapse.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.910
A very talented YouTuber did,

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.772
and he deserves a medal for it.

00:00:43.772 --> 00:00:45.000
(fanfare music)

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.340
Or perhaps just a new patron. Thanks, man.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.610
Anyway, the most recent
carving up of this region

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.920
happened by European powers,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.720
the French, the British, the Russians.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.180
I mean, are we surprised? No.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.800
Like, of course. Of
course it was the British.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.670
Of course it was the French.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.080
Of course it was Europeans. Of course.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.530
The lines they drew didn't
really take into account language

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.680
or ethnicity or regional identity.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.500
They just sort of sliced it
all up amongst themselves

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.040
and said, "These are
our new regions of power

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.120
in the Middle East."

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.190
Eventually, those European powers left,

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:21.720
but the lines they drew stuck
around and became the skeleton

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.910
for what the borders look like today.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.040
And this is where our story starts,

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.430
in the 1930s, here in
the modern Middle East.

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.830
At this point, across the ocean,

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.720
there was this growing superpower

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.210
that had spent the last
century moving west,

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.910
taking over this whole
continent and beyond,

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.260
deep into the Pacific Ocean.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.450
We've talked about that a bit.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.980
But things were changing.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:47.250
The world had just
fought a brutal world war

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.200
that was fought with new weapons

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.190
that were powered by this
new important substance, oil.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.870
Germany lost that war,

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.230
in part because they didn't
have access to enough oil

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.750
to keep up with this new style of warfare

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.900
that relied a lot more on machines.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.900
The young superpower realized
that access to this stuff

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.020
would determine who would be
powerful and who would not.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.950
So they stopped looking west
for a moment and turned east,

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.080
with hopes of finding the fuel they needed

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.430
to build their power.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.170
The U.S. presence in
the Middle East started

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.510
with one little dot, right here.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:24.780
But soon, that dot would
expand into a sprawling network

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:29.490
of alliances, covert attacks,
flows of weapons, money,

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.890
and the building of innumerable bases,

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.543
and eventually turning
into full-on ground wars.

00:02:34.543 --> 00:02:36.780
(intriguing music)

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.354
This is how the U.S.
stole the Middle East.

00:02:39.354 --> 00:02:40.187
(intriguing music)

00:02:40.187 --> 00:02:44.608
- Ready and willing to
employ all means necessary.

00:02:44.608 --> 00:02:46.377
- Okay, so it's the 1930s

00:02:46.377 --> 00:02:49.260
and the U.S. doesn't have
a significant presence

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.550
in the Middle East at this point.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:51.720
But that's about to change,

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.910
because there's a company
based in California

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.390
that wants to explore
this vast desert for oil.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:00.630
- [Narrator] 11,000
miles from San Francisco

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:03.030
there lies a primeval desert,

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.210
a mass of drifting sand
and sun-baked earth,

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.610
one third the size of the United States.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.110
- [Johnny] This was
sort of a risky decision

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:11.910
for the California company
because, first off,

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:15.060
they had no idea if there
was actually any oil here.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:15.930
- [Narrator] They knew it would mean

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:17.160
sinking into the desert

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.500
the money of thousands of stockholders

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.620
in a project that might
well end in complete loss.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.990
- [Johnny] And second off,
this desert was a part

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:28.620
of a very hardcore religious kingdom.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.480
- [Narrator] The fact
that Mecca is the source

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.500
and the shrine of Islam gives
Saudi Arabia a central place

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.350
in the Islamic and,
therefore, the Arab world.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.990
- [Johnny] that was home to
the holiest sites in Islam,

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:44.100
run by a dogmatic royal family
that did not like outsiders,

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.230
especially non-believing Westerners.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.380
But even still, the king
of the desert kingdom

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.810
eventually gives the
California company permission

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.750
to explore almost a
million square kilometers

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.030
of this desert looking for oil.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:59.910
And after a few years, the bet paid off.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.340
And on March 3rd, 1938,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.120
in this little patch of coastal
desert, they struck gold.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.590
Well, actually they struck oil,

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.886
but it might as well have been gold.

00:04:09.886 --> 00:04:12.553
(kinetic music)

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:18.750
So, throughout the '30s and
'40s, American oil executives,

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.370
workers, and their families

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.380
started flocking to the Middle East,

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.350
establishing the first
significant American presence

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:26.183
in the region.

00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:28.980
They set up little cities
around the oil operation

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:31.200
that were little slices of America,

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.410
full of the deepest sinful behavior,

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:38.820
like allowing women to drive
and the consumption of alcohol.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.590
- [Narrator] Here is
another American colony,

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.520
complete with air-conditioned
houses, two hospitals,

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.350
and an outdoor movie theater.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:49.320
- This is the sort of stuff
that is very off-limits

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:50.153
in Saudi Arabia.

00:04:50.153 --> 00:04:51.960
It's literally illegal at this point.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.910
So you have a lot of
Saudis who are not happy

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:56.490
about their government
letting the Americans in

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.080
to behave however they want.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.490
But the oil kept flowing,

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:02.190
and soon, the U.S. government
goes to the royal family

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:05.400
and says, "Listen, the oil
is flowing better than ever.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.510
This is awesome.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:09.060
How about we build a little military base

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.950
attached to our little oil city

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.230
so that we can, you know, protect you

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.840
and protect us and protect
the oil and stuff?"

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.660
And the Saudis are like, "Okay.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:20.340
Having the great Satan come to our country

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.990
for oil is one thing,

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:25.815
but letting them set up a full-on
military base on our soil,

00:05:25.815 --> 00:05:26.648
(John inhales sharply)

00:05:26.648 --> 00:05:28.560
and especially when, like,
everyone in our country

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.937
is not happy with their
presence in the first place.

00:05:30.937 --> 00:05:34.177
"But," said the royal family,

00:05:34.177 --> 00:05:36.540
"all of this oil is really valuable,

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.580
and it's really nice, and
we're getting super rich."

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.770
So they're like, "Yeah,
sure. Set up the base."

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.270
But there was one stipulation

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.747
that the Saudis had for the Americans.

00:05:43.747 --> 00:05:46.890
"You are not allowed to
literally plant a flag.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:48.930
No flag poles of the United States.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.540
You cannot put your flag
anywhere on this base.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.880
Instead, you can put a little plaque

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:54.840
on the side of the building

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.240
so that your flag is not
literally on our soil."

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.730
And that was the deal. And
that's exactly what happened.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:03.480
The U.S. sets up its
first military operation

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:06.240
in the Middle East in the
form of a landing strip

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.864
that is right next to this oil field.

00:06:07.864 --> 00:06:10.290
(plane engine roaring)

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.270
Okay, so all of this infrastructure

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.950
that the Americans were building

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:16.050
required someone to build it.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.180
They needed a construction company.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.770
And there was one construction company

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.090
that the Americans really liked

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.730
that helped them build their
oil city and their base.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:27.600
This company was founded and
run by a guy named Mohammed.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.340
Now, listen, do you think
I'm really giving you

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:31.410
the backstory on the construction company

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.360
that built the air base in the oil city

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.633
just because that's interesting

00:06:34.633 --> 00:06:37.020
and I like to talk about construction?

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.600
No, this is actually very
relevant to the story,

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.550
and you'll see why very soon.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.350
So the Americans and the Saudis are having

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:47.400
this forbidden oil bromance
and it's going really well,

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.570
and they are just,

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.210
the oil is flowing,
everyone's getting rich.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.970
And meanwhile the rest of the Middle East

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:57.690
is looking at Saudi Arabia
and they're like, "Dude, WTF.

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:00.210
Why are you like in bed with America?

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:02.160
And, like, why are you letting them set up

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.440
a landing strip in your country?"

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.277
And the Saudi royals are like,

00:07:06.277 --> 00:07:08.490
"Do you realize how rich
we're getting right now?

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.020
Like if you were in our position,

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:12.300
you would do the same thing, Egypt."

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:13.740
Okay, so it's the 1950s

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.560
and let's get back to
Mohammed, the construction guy.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.350
His company, by this point, is thriving.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:23.400
The American presence in
oil land is just exploding

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.647
and he is building all
of the stuff for it.

00:07:25.647 --> 00:07:29.040
And so this guy just has a giant business.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.870
And he starts to have children.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.760
Well, in fact, he had a lot of children,

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:36.510
like 54 children because he had 22 wives,

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:40.920
because that is a thing in
Saudi Arabia to this day.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:45.062
Anyway, the point is one of
Mohammed's sons is named Osama.

00:07:45.062 --> 00:07:48.729
(downbeat electronic music)

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.780
I told you this was going to be relevant.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.240
Okay, a reminder that Saudi Arabia

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.810
is not the entire Middle East.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:55.830
So, I'm going to leave

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.770
the Osama bin Laden
cliffhanger for a moment

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.150
to tell you what else was going on

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:01.410
in the Middle East at this time.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.450
Remember that it was the hunt for oil

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.600
that brought the U.S. to
Saudi Arabia originally.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:10.290
But now in the '50s and
'60s, there was a new reason

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.600
for the U.S. to think
about the Middle East.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:15.840
And that reason is because
there's another big superpower

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.870
that has nuclear weapons
called the Soviet Union,

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:21.997
who is coming into the region
and saying to everyone,

00:08:21.997 --> 00:08:24.150
"Come join team communism."

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.533
And the U.S. is like, "Hold my beer."

00:08:26.533 --> 00:08:29.283
(dramatic music)

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.830
So in addition to oil, the
U.S. is now involved in trying

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:38.670
to not let the Soviet Union
have any power in this region.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:41.610
Over in Iran, there was a
democratically-elected leader

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:42.960
that the U.S. didn't like.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.240
They thought he was maybe
a little too friendly

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:46.290
with the Soviet Union.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.270
So they worked together with the British

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:51.780
to literally overthrow
the government of Iran

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:54.960
so that they could install
a dictatorial leader

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.780
that was more friendly
to the United States.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:58.950
Little side note here.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.920
The airport that I fly out of here in D.C.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:05.220
is named after the guy who,
like, gave the go ahead

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:08.340
for this coup in Iran, John Foster Dulles.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:11.400
So, I'm reminded of the whole
Iran thing every time I fly.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.570
So the U.S. has its oil thing.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:16.050
It's now involved in trying
to prop up a dictator in Iran.

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:17.340
There's another big thing happening

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.110
that brings the U.S. into the region,

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:22.620
which is that the newly
declared State of Israel

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.930
is starting to piss off its neighbors

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.690
and starting to look to
the U.S. for support.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:30.360
And the U.S. gladly offers it,

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:34.440
seeing Israel as a friendly
nation in the region

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:38.010
that could be a big
proponent of U.S. interests.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:41.220
So the U.S. starts to fund
Israel with tons of money

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.740
and fighter jets, and all of these things

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:46.590
to help them fight their wars
against their Arab neighbors.

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.510
There was a debate happening
in the United States

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:50.460
on whether or not they should
actually do all of this

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.470
to support Israel so intensely,

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.810
because they knew if they did,
they were going to piss off

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:57.000
all of the neighbors in the Middle East.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.460
And all of the neighbors are
the ones who had the oil.

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:02.220
In the end, the U.S. did
decide to support Israel,

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:04.950
and with that, came a major backlash

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.530
from all of these oil-producing countries

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:08.370
in the neighborhood.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.870
- There's a crisis of such proportion

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.120
that we probably haven't
even begun to grasp it yet

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:13.710
as far as the country is concerned.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:15.810
- [Narrator] Scenes like this
are becoming all too common

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:17.580
on both sides of the Atlantic.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:20.220
But for America, they are more ominous.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:22.110
They tell the Arabs that their oil weapon

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:23.160
is wounding America,

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:26.220
the country that supports and
supplies their enemy, Israel.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:28.920
- Eventually, this backlash
against supporting Israel

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.910
kind of calmed down.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.200
There was some peace talks.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:32.910
And anyway, let's get back to Mohammed,

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:35.100
the construction guy, and his son Osama,

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:38.400
because this is where it
really starts to heat up.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:40.290
We decided to put
together this compilation

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:41.700
of all our Middle East videos

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:45.480
because there are
transformative events happening

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:46.470
in the Middle East right now.

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.500
The recent attacks on Iran
from the U.S. and Israel

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.570
have reshaped the Middle East

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:53.880
and are doing that right
now as I'm recording this.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:54.840
And hopefully these videos

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.250
are providing some context,

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:57.930
but keeping up with the headlines

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:59.610
is proving to be really difficult

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:03.210
because every source comes
at it with a different angle

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:04.500
and a different bias.

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:07.470
This is why I have
partnered with Ground News.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.660
They are the sponsor of this compilation.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.420
And I've been using Ground
News for over a year now.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.890
They've been a partner of the channel

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:15.270
and I'm really grateful they exist.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.010
Ground News is an app and a website

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.590
that allows you to very
quickly and thoroughly

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:22.470
compare thousands of headlines
from all around the world.

