00:13:08.094 --> 00:13:11.010
- So it's now the '70s,
and Mohammed bin Laden,

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:14.640
the construction guy,
is now insanely rich.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.350
His construction company is giant,

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:18.690
his 54 children are also rich,

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:23.010
and his son Osama is growing
up, and he is in his twenties,

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.920
and is looking around at
all of this stuff happening

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.920
in Iran and in Israel,

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:32.310
and is starting to feel
really uncomfortable

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:35.250
with the notion of his
family being so supportive

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:36.900
of American presence in the Middle East

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:39.120
and his government,
this religious kingdom,

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:43.230
home of Mecca and Medina,
being so okay with the U.S.

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:45.697
so embedded in the Middle
East at this point.

00:13:45.697 --> 00:13:48.480
"These are ancient holy lands.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.330
Why is my government and my family

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:54.990
supporting this great
Satan superpower coming in

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:57.240
and becoming so involved
in the Middle East?"

00:13:57.240 --> 00:14:00.840
So, Bin Laden sets out on a lifelong quest

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.450
to fight back against these superpowers,

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:05.730
not just the U.S. but
also the Soviet Union,

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:07.680
invading the Middle East.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.120
He heads to Afghanistan,

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.820
where the Soviet Union
is invading Afghanistan,

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:12.870
trying to take it over.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.610
Bin Laden wants to fight back.

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:17.070
By the way, the same year in Iran,

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:20.400
that dictator that the
U.S. put in gets overthrown

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:23.040
in a giant religious revolution

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:26.010
that gets rid of the old
dictator that the U.S. liked

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.380
and puts in a religious government

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:31.380
headed by this guy, Ayatollah Khomeini.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:34.110
This new government takes a
bunch of Americans hostage

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:37.140
and starts off hating the United States.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.910
And I mean, can you blame them?

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.040
If someone overthrew the person I elected,

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.480
I would be pretty pissed too.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.860
So anyway, back to Bin Laden.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.410
He arrives to Afghanistan
with a few things.

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:48.570
Number one, a bunch of money.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.580
Remember his family's like super rich.

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:53.190
He also comes with
construction infrastructure

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:55.230
because he's, like, a construction guy.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:56.730
Like, his family knows construction

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:58.050
and infrastructure building.

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:02.130
But most importantly, he comes
with an obsessive dedication

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.740
to fighting back against any superpower

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:06.360
that is invading the Middle East.

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:09.593
So, Osama joins in with
all of these rebel fighters

00:15:09.593 --> 00:15:12.150
who are fighting back
against the Soviet Union,

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:15.180
and they fight a long, brutal war.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.310
By the way, the U.S. was
secretly loving this,

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:20.580
loving that the Soviet Union
was getting, like, beat back

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.530
by these, like, rebel fighters.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:25.380
So they end up sending
loads of weapons and money

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.450
and support to these fighters,

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:29.970
something that will come back to bite them

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:31.140
a few decades later.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:34.350
Eventually, Osama and the Afghan fighters

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:36.450
beat back the Soviet Union.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:38.340
It was 10 brutal years of war,

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:42.060
and by the end, these
fighters were battle hardened.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:45.540
Osama was now completely
dedicated to his cause

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.850
of fighting back against superpowers

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:49.560
who were coming into the Middle East.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:52.080
So he returns back to Saudi Arabia,

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.840
where he starts raising
money and awareness

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.010
for his new group

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:58.140
that he started while
he was in Afghanistan.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:15:59.700
It's called Al-Qaeda.

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:02.850
And the mission of the
group is to protect Islam

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:06.630
through violently striking
back against big superpowers

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.220
coming into the Middle East.

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:09.403
And Saudi Arabia is like,

00:16:09.403 --> 00:16:11.550
"(sighs) Osama, like, do
you have to do this, dude?

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.170
Do you realize how rich we're getting?"

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:15.510
Like, Saudi princes are living on yachts

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:16.500
in the south of France

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.000
and, like, flying in their private jets

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.980
and they're like, "Dude, chill.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:21.420
Like, it's fine. We get it.

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.440
We don't like the United States,

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:24.480
but, like, can you, like, maybe chill?

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:25.830
Our partnership with the United States

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.390
is actually turning
out to be really great.

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:29.340
And I know, yeah, they're
really into Israel

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:30.570
and they're really bad and everything,

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:33.750
but, like, they buy our oil
and they give us weapons

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:36.930
and we're, like, doing
just fine over here."

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.490
Osama doesn't chill,

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:41.580
and the Saudi government
eventually takes away his passport,

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.770
not letting him leave,
and told him to hush up

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:46.170
with all the anti-American Holy War talk.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:48.480
So, Osama finds another plan

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:51.337
to maybe win back the heart of the royals.

00:16:51.337 --> 00:16:53.754
(dark music)

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.720
Saudi Arabia has a next-door
neighbor named Iraq,

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:00.180
who was run by Saddam Hussein,

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:02.670
who Osama sees as a really bad Muslim,

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:04.560
totally secular and brutal,

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:06.330
and he's just like not a good guy.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.850
Saddam is also cashing in on the oil boom.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:11.370
He's building big palaces
and statues of himself

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:12.600
all over the country.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:14.220
Oh yeah, and he also used the oil money

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:15.810
to build a giant army,

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:18.180
like, the fourth biggest in the world.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:21.060
With this massive army, Saddam decided

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:24.180
that he could maybe
multiply his oil reserves

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.290
if he popped down

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:28.350
to invade this little
tiny country of Kuwait,

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:30.090
where there's also loads of oil.

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:31.950
This sort of freaked the Saudis out.

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:35.340
If Saddam with his giant
army could grab Kuwait,

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:38.550
what would stop him from
marching right across this desert

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:40.020
into Saudi Arabia?

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:42.270
So there's this moment that, like,

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:45.210
ugh, it's like the moment of
infamy of this whole thing,

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:48.180
where Osama goes to the
Saudis and he says...

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:50.310
- I volunteer as tribute.

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:52.230
- He doesn't actually say,
"I volunteer in tribute."

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:53.922
That was "Hunger Games."

00:17:53.922 --> 00:17:55.560
- I believe we have a volunteer.

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:56.947
- But he effectively says,

00:17:56.947 --> 00:17:59.580
"I have me and my battle-hardened men

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:02.010
who, like, can go in
and fight against Saddam

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:04.830
and defend the kingdom."

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:08.190
And the Saudis are like,
"Um, no, we're not gonna,

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:12.030
like, let this ragtag group
of, like, rebel fighters

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.700
fight off the fourth-largest
army in the world."

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:17.760
And Osama's like, "Well,
we beat the Soviets.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:18.630
Like, they're a big army

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:20.040
with nuclear weapons and everything."

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:20.917
And the Saudis are like,

00:18:20.917 --> 00:18:23.370
"Yeah, because you hid in the hills,

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.320
in caves, in Afghanistan."

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:29.407
Prince Sultan literally told
Bin Laden verbatim, quote,

00:18:29.407 --> 00:18:32.730
"There are no caves in Kuwait."

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:34.057
And then he asks them,

00:18:34.057 --> 00:18:36.750
"What will you do when he
lobs the missiles at you

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:39.150
with chemical and biological weapons?"

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:42.951
Osama's response, "We will
fight them with our faith."

00:18:42.951 --> 00:18:43.784
(sinking music)

00:18:43.784 --> 00:18:48.000
And the Saudis are like, "Um, awkward.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:50.370
Sorry, dude. Like... (scoffs)"

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:52.320
Instead the king met with somebody else

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:55.170
that he thought would
make a much better fit

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:57.430
than Bin Laden and his faith fighters.

00:18:57.430 --> 00:19:00.180
(dramatic music)

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.330
Dick Cheney had flown to Saudi Arabia

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:06.270
the day after Saddam had invaded Kuwait.

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:08.247
At this point, the
bromance between the U.S.

00:19:08.247 --> 00:19:10.320
and Saudi Arabia had cooled a little bit

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.540
as Saudi had gotten more and more flak

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.670
for being in bed with the U.S.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:17.490
But even despite this,
he told Cheney to come

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:20.643
with as much force and
as quickly as he could.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:26.010
And that is exactly what Dick Cheney did.

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:30.767
- Ready and willing to
employ all means necessary.

00:19:30.767 --> 00:19:34.350
(explosion booms faintly)

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:38.040
- The U.S. went insane here.

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:40.350
They recruited 37 other countries,

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:42.450
and then they sent more firepower

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.750
in terms of ships and bombers and troops

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:48.270
