00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.660
and dive into each of these cases

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:56.820
to show how the U.S.
presence in the Middle East

00:21:56.820 --> 00:21:58.560
is not just about oil.

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:01.620
In fact, oil is becoming less
and less of a vital aspect

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:02.640
of the U.S. presence

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:05.730
as we have alternative sources
of this sort of energy.

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:07.890
Instead, our presence in
the Middle East has become

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:10.710
a fixture of how we think
about foreign policy

00:22:10.710 --> 00:22:12.540
and how we think about the map.

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:15.750
It's become so embedded
in our military doctrine

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:17.450
and in our foreign policy doctrine

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:20.820
that it's proving to be really hard

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:22.870
to think about how we could ever get out.

00:22:31.121 --> 00:22:32.190
(soft dramatic music)

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:33.630
One of the most important wars

00:22:33.630 --> 00:22:36.720
