00:42:01.185 --> 00:42:03.935
(dramatic music)

00:42:06.556 --> 00:42:09.556
(keyboard clicking)

00:42:12.840 --> 00:42:14.370
In the summer of 2002,

00:42:14.370 --> 00:42:17.370
the Director of the British
Intelligence Agency, MI6,

00:42:17.370 --> 00:42:20.250
Richard Dearlove, traveled
to Washington D.C.

00:42:20.250 --> 00:42:23.430
to meet with the Director
of the CIA, George Tenet.

00:42:23.430 --> 00:42:25.290
The topic of the meeting was Iraq

00:42:25.290 --> 00:42:27.090
and its leader, Saddam Hussein.

00:42:27.090 --> 00:42:27.923
In the meeting,

00:42:27.923 --> 00:42:30.240
the CIA director shared
classified information

00:42:30.240 --> 00:42:31.950
with his British counterpart,

00:42:31.950 --> 00:42:35.490
who then traveled back to
London to 10 Downing Street,

00:42:35.490 --> 00:42:37.893
the home of the Prime
Minister, Tony Blair.

00:42:38.880 --> 00:42:41.100
Dearlove told his Prime
Minister everything

00:42:41.100 --> 00:42:43.380
about what was really
happening behind the scenes

00:42:43.380 --> 00:42:44.790
in the United States,

00:42:44.790 --> 00:42:48.180
how the U.S. was planning to
invade Iraq no matter what.

00:42:48.180 --> 00:42:49.950
It was a highly classified meeting

00:42:49.950 --> 00:42:53.400
but notes were taken and
classified and put into a memo.

00:42:53.400 --> 00:42:54.960
That memo was later leaked

00:42:54.960 --> 00:42:57.240
to British author and
journalist, Michael Smith,

00:42:57.240 --> 00:42:59.220
who published it in 2005

00:42:59.220 --> 00:43:00.810
and that's what we're looking at,

00:43:00.810 --> 00:43:03.690
a secret meeting and the memo it produced,

00:43:03.690 --> 00:43:06.990
meant only for the eyes
of top British officials.

00:43:06.990 --> 00:43:08.970
It was an explosive leak.

00:43:08.970 --> 00:43:11.730
What we see is that Dearlove
tells his Prime Minister

00:43:11.730 --> 00:43:14.400
everything he heard in
Washington a few days earlier,

00:43:14.400 --> 00:43:16.290
and that this was a very different story

00:43:16.290 --> 00:43:17.970
than the one the Bush administration

00:43:17.970 --> 00:43:19.260
was telling to the public,

00:43:19.260 --> 00:43:21.540
that an American invasion was inevitable,

00:43:21.540 --> 00:43:23.190
that Bush's people were fixated

00:43:23.190 --> 00:43:26.310
on removing Saddam Hussein
from power, no matter what,

00:43:26.310 --> 00:43:27.390
and that the U.S. government

00:43:27.390 --> 00:43:29.940
was blatantly cooking up intel and facts

00:43:29.940 --> 00:43:31.950
to help sell their invasion.

00:43:31.950 --> 00:43:35.730
This document shows us how
power really works in our world,

00:43:35.730 --> 00:43:39.120
how a small group of people
decided to topple a dictator,

00:43:39.120 --> 00:43:40.710
to occupy a country,

00:43:40.710 --> 00:43:43.590
and then invented a story
to support their plan.

00:43:43.590 --> 00:43:44.910
It was a false story,

00:43:44.910 --> 00:43:47.640
but it helped them sell a horrifying war.

00:43:47.640 --> 00:43:50.850
It's a story that is revealed in detail

00:43:50.850 --> 00:43:52.294
by the Downing Street memo.

00:43:52.294 --> 00:43:53.130
(dramatic music continues)

00:43:53.130 --> 00:43:56.700
- States like these
constitute an axis of evil.

00:43:56.700 --> 00:43:58.980
One last chance to avoid war.

00:43:58.980 --> 00:44:00.791
And the entire world will know

00:44:00.791 --> 00:44:04.788
that we will take whatever
actions necessary.

00:44:04.788 --> 00:44:07.410
On September the 11th, enemies of freedom

00:44:07.410 --> 00:44:09.600
committed an act of war
against our country.

00:44:09.600 --> 00:44:12.090
The United States
military has begun strikes

00:44:12.090 --> 00:44:15.360
against Al-Qaeda terrorist
training camps in Afghanistan.

00:44:15.360 --> 00:44:16.320
- [Johnny] Let's start by looking

00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:19.140
at another document from the fall of 2001

00:44:19.140 --> 00:44:21.660
when Deputy Secretary of
Defense Paul Wolfowitz

00:44:21.660 --> 00:44:24.660
created this memo for his
boss, Donald Rumsfeld,

00:44:24.660 --> 00:44:26.610
the Secretary of Defense.

00:44:26.610 --> 00:44:28.800
This was just 10 weeks after the attacks

00:44:28.800 --> 00:44:30.780
that changed the course of history

00:44:30.780 --> 00:44:32.790
but this document wasn't about that.

00:44:32.790 --> 00:44:34.350
It was about Iraq,

00:44:34.350 --> 00:44:36.900
a country that had
nothing to do with 9/11.

00:44:36.900 --> 00:44:38.340
Rumsfeld reviewed the document

00:44:38.340 --> 00:44:40.290
before meeting with an army general.

00:44:40.290 --> 00:44:41.910
He marked it up with his notes,

00:44:41.910 --> 00:44:43.260
giving us insight into

00:44:43.260 --> 00:44:45.690
what the Secretary of
Defense of the United States

00:44:45.690 --> 00:44:48.000
was really thinking about after 9/11,

00:44:48.000 --> 00:44:49.470
how this group of military leaders

00:44:49.470 --> 00:44:51.750
were set on, quote, "building momentum"

00:44:51.750 --> 00:44:54.240
to topple Iraq's dictator, Saddam Hussein,

00:44:54.240 --> 00:44:56.070
to decapitate the government,

00:44:56.070 --> 00:44:58.710
a government that was no
longer useful to them.

00:44:58.710 --> 00:45:01.080
Saddam Hussein had been a useful client

00:45:01.080 --> 00:45:03.240
to the United States,
especially in the '80s

00:45:03.240 --> 00:45:05.610
when he was waging a war against Iran,

00:45:05.610 --> 00:45:07.620
an enemy of the United States.

00:45:07.620 --> 00:45:09.300
But those days were now over.

00:45:09.300 --> 00:45:11.970
Saddam had turned into just
a troublemaker in the region,

00:45:11.970 --> 00:45:13.860
creating instability that could threaten

00:45:13.860 --> 00:45:16.290
the U.S.' easy access to oil.

00:45:16.290 --> 00:45:19.710
- Two hours ago, allied
air forces began an attack

00:45:19.710 --> 00:45:22.320
on military targets in Iraq and Kuwait.

00:45:22.320 --> 00:45:24.600
This conflict started August 2nd

00:45:24.600 --> 00:45:25.950
when the dictator of Iraq

00:45:25.950 --> 00:45:28.740
invaded a small and helpless neighbor.

00:45:28.740 --> 00:45:31.260
- [Johnny] And in many
ways, Iraq was an old mess

00:45:31.260 --> 00:45:32.790
in need of cleaning up,

00:45:32.790 --> 00:45:35.370
a mess that Bush Senior
had failed to resolve

00:45:35.370 --> 00:45:36.960
during the first Gulf War.

00:45:36.960 --> 00:45:39.450
Iraq was supposed to disarm
itself after that war

00:45:39.450 --> 00:45:42.429
but had kicked out the UN
weapons inspector teams.

00:45:42.429 --> 00:45:43.740
(brooding music)

00:45:43.740 --> 00:45:46.290
But that wasn't the main
reason why, right after 9/11,

00:45:46.290 --> 00:45:48.570
these guys were talking
about invading Iraq.

00:45:48.570 --> 00:45:50.820
A bigger reason is that
these leaders wanted

00:45:50.820 --> 00:45:54.090
to remind the world who
the global superpower was.

00:45:54.090 --> 00:45:54.960
They needed to

00:45:54.960 --> 00:45:57.780
after being brutally
attacked on their own soil.

00:45:57.780 --> 00:46:00.240
A non-U.S.-friendly regime, like Iraq,

00:46:00.240 --> 00:46:03.420
couldn't be allowed to
stand in a post 9/11 world,

00:46:03.420 --> 00:46:05.580
or in the words of Rumsfeld himself,

00:46:05.580 --> 00:46:07.740
hours after the towers fell,

00:46:07.740 --> 00:46:10.500
quote, "We need to bomb something else

00:46:10.500 --> 00:46:12.480
to show that we're big and strong

00:46:12.480 --> 00:46:14.820
and not gonna be pushed around."

00:46:14.820 --> 00:46:17.583
Iraq and its leader was
that something else.

00:46:18.810 --> 00:46:21.330
And now, Bush and his advisors
were looking at a plan

00:46:21.330 --> 00:46:22.860
to make it a reality.

00:46:22.860 --> 00:46:24.300
But how to start the war?

00:46:24.300 --> 00:46:25.650
Could they tie Saddam Hussein

00:46:25.650 --> 00:46:29.580
to something that Americans
feared, like 9/11 or anthrax?

00:46:29.580 --> 00:46:30.660
Or could they tell a story

00:46:30.660 --> 00:46:32.700
about weapons of mass destruction?

00:46:32.700 --> 00:46:34.380
What other countries could they bring in

00:46:34.380 --> 00:46:35.940
to support their invasion?

00:46:35.940 --> 00:46:38.250
And, of course, the most
important consideration,

00:46:38.250 --> 00:46:40.290
Rumsfeld jots it here at the end,

00:46:40.290 --> 00:46:42.420
they would need an influence campaign,

00:46:42.420 --> 00:46:44.190
they would need to sell the war.

00:46:44.190 --> 00:46:46.110
And when should they begin?

00:46:46.110 --> 00:46:47.381
How about right away?

00:46:47.381 --> 00:46:48.900
(intense music)

00:46:48.900 --> 00:46:50.850
- Iraq continues to flaunt his hostility

00:46:50.850 --> 00:46:52.740
toward America and to support terror.

00:46:52.740 --> 00:46:53.573
- [Johnny] Three months later,

00:46:53.573 --> 00:46:54.810
the President was telling the world

00:46:54.810 --> 00:46:57.690
that Iraq was one of a
group of evil countries

00:46:57.690 --> 00:46:59.160
that the U.S. must oppose

00:46:59.160 --> 00:47:01.080
in the global fight against good and evil.

00:47:01.080 --> 00:47:04.260
- States like these
constitute an axis of evil.

00:47:04.260 --> 00:47:07.380
The price of indifference
would be catastrophic.

00:47:07.380 --> 00:47:08.970
- [Johnny] By the summer of 2002,

00:47:08.970 --> 00:47:12.480
this idea that Bush's advisors
had scratched down after 9/11

00:47:12.480 --> 00:47:14.850
was developing into an official policy.

00:47:14.850 --> 00:47:17.130
That handwritten influence campaign

00:47:17.130 --> 00:47:19.650
to sell the war was now in full swing.

00:47:19.650 --> 00:47:21.780
- There is no doubt that Saddam Hussein

00:47:21.780 --> 00:47:23.700
now has weapons of mass destruction.

00:47:23.700 --> 00:47:25.380
- The Iraqi regime has been free

00:47:25.380 --> 00:47:27.870
to pursue the development of
weapons of mass destruction.

00:47:27.870 --> 00:47:30.120
- We know they have weapons
of mass destruction,

00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:31.950
there isn't any debate about it.

00:47:31.950 --> 00:47:34.290
- [Johnny] And this is
exactly what the head of MI6

00:47:34.290 --> 00:47:36.570
told Prime Minister
Tony Blair at his house

00:47:36.570 --> 00:47:37.950
in the summer of 2002

00:47:37.950 --> 00:47:40.200
after meeting with the CIA in Washington.

00:47:40.200 --> 00:47:42.300
It's what we see in
the Downing Street memo

00:47:42.300 --> 00:47:46.230
that there was a perceptible
shift in attitude in Washington

00:47:46.230 --> 00:47:48.270
and that the U.S. invasion of Iraq

00:47:48.270 --> 00:47:50.190
was now seen as inevitable

00:47:50.190 --> 00:47:52.590
and that they were now fixing intelligence

00:47:52.590 --> 00:47:55.020
around a decision that
they had already made,

00:47:55.020 --> 00:47:56.760
and that the U.S. wasn't really planning

00:47:56.760 --> 00:47:58.170
to work with the UN.

00:47:58.170 --> 00:47:59.850
They didn't want weapons inspections

00:47:59.850 --> 00:48:02.640
or getting UN approval
for a military force.

00:48:02.640 --> 00:48:06.240
And crucially, the head of the
MI6 tells the Prime Minister

00:48:06.240 --> 00:48:08.850
that these Bush people
aren't really thinking much

00:48:08.850 --> 00:48:10.893
about the aftermath of such an invasion.

00:48:12.900 --> 00:48:14.940
- What is inevitable is not regime change,

00:48:14.940 --> 00:48:17.092
it is disarmament of
weapons of mass destruction.

00:48:17.092 --> 00:48:18.000
(subdued music)

00:48:18.000 --> 00:48:19.170
- [Johnny] This memo wasn't supposed

00:48:19.170 --> 00:48:21.540
to be seen by anyone but just a few,

00:48:21.540 --> 00:48:23.400
and that's why we can learn from it.

00:48:23.400 --> 00:48:26.130
It serves as one of the most
potent pieces of evidence

00:48:26.130 --> 00:48:27.270
that the Bush administration

00:48:27.270 --> 00:48:30.030
was maneuvering two
very different stories.

00:48:30.030 --> 00:48:31.830
Their private story about the need

00:48:31.830 --> 00:48:34.740
to remove a dictator
to project U.S. power,

00:48:34.740 --> 00:48:37.140
which was in stark contrast
to the public story

00:48:37.140 --> 00:48:39.300
that they had to tell
to sell the invasion,

00:48:39.300 --> 00:48:41.040
their influence campaign.

00:48:41.040 --> 00:48:42.900
- Any country on the face of the earth

00:48:42.900 --> 00:48:44.850
with an active intelligence program

00:48:44.850 --> 00:48:47.670
knows that Iraq has weapons
of mass destruction.

00:48:47.670 --> 00:48:48.503
- [Johnny] Because they knew

00:48:48.503 --> 00:48:50.310
that if they were really
gonna sell this war,

00:48:50.310 --> 00:48:52.950
they would need to convince
not only the American public

00:48:52.950 --> 00:48:55.470
but also Congress and at least partially,

00:48:55.470 --> 00:48:57.000
the international community.

00:48:57.000 --> 00:48:58.710
What we learned in the Downing Street memo

00:48:58.710 --> 00:48:59.700
is that they had settled

00:48:59.700 --> 00:49:02.460
on two main focus points for their story,

00:49:02.460 --> 00:49:04.860
that Iraq has weapons of mass destruction

00:49:04.860 --> 00:49:08.010
and that they're also working
with the masterminds of 9/11.

00:49:08.010 --> 00:49:11.430
Not long after this meeting
between MI6 and the CIA,

00:49:11.430 --> 00:49:14.820
Bush and his allies ramp
up their influence campaign

00:49:14.820 --> 00:49:16.650
to sell their war.

00:49:16.650 --> 00:49:19.560
- We've learned that Iraq
has trained Al-Qaeda members

00:49:19.560 --> 00:49:22.620
in bomb making, poisons, and deadly gases.

00:49:22.620 --> 00:49:24.240
- [Johnny] The sales pitches
to the American people

00:49:24.240 --> 00:49:27.570
for an invasion of Iraq were
made with absolute certainty.

00:49:27.570 --> 00:49:30.000
Certainty that Iraq had WMDs.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:32.130
- He had agreed, and the UN had agreed,

00:49:32.130 --> 00:49:34.860
that he would not have a WMD program.

00:49:34.860 --> 00:49:36.150
We know he does have one.

00:49:36.150 --> 00:49:38.130
- [Johnny] Certainty that
they wanted to use them

00:49:38.130 --> 00:49:40.470
against Americans and American allies.

00:49:40.470 --> 00:49:43.113
- Simply stated, there is no doubt

00:49:43.113 --> 00:49:46.530
that Saddam Hussein now has
weapons of mass destruction,

00:49:46.530 --> 00:49:49.770
that he is amassing them
to use against our friends,

00:49:49.770 --> 00:49:51.960
against our allies, and against us.

00:49:51.960 --> 00:49:54.660
- [Johnny] Certainty that
Iraq was harboring terrorists.

00:49:54.660 --> 00:49:57.720
- An Al-Qaeda terrorist
escaped from Afghanistan

00:49:57.720 --> 00:49:59.790
and are known to be in Iraq.

00:49:59.790 --> 00:50:01.080
- [Johnny] And certainty that Iraq

00:50:01.080 --> 00:50:03.600
was working on obtaining nuclear weapons.

00:50:03.600 --> 00:50:05.070
- And Iraq's state-controlled media

00:50:05.070 --> 00:50:07.050
has reported numerous meetings

00:50:07.050 --> 00:50:10.290
between Saddam Hussein and
his nuclear scientists,

00:50:10.290 --> 00:50:11.670
leaving little doubt

00:50:11.670 --> 00:50:15.150
about his continued
appetite for these weapons.

00:50:15.150 --> 00:50:16.860
- [Johnny] And these
speeches were working.

00:50:16.860 --> 00:50:19.740
By the fall of 2002,
Americans were in favor

00:50:19.740 --> 00:50:22.620
of an invasion of Iraq by
just a narrow majority.

00:50:22.620 --> 00:50:24.510
But there was just one problem,

00:50:24.510 --> 00:50:27.852
that all of these statements were lies.

00:50:27.852 --> 00:50:29.460
(moody music)

00:50:29.460 --> 00:50:31.500
Indeed, this was already known

00:50:31.500 --> 00:50:33.690
in the secret rooms of Downing Street

00:50:33.690 --> 00:50:36.750
that the U.S. was fixing
their facts and their intel

00:50:36.750 --> 00:50:39.150
to match their already-made decision.

00:50:39.150 --> 00:50:40.920
Iraq's supposed links to Al-Qaeda

00:50:40.920 --> 00:50:43.590
were based on one interrogation of a guy

00:50:43.590 --> 00:50:46.710
whose testimony lacked,
quote, "specific details"

00:50:46.710 --> 00:50:48.690
and who was intentionally lying about it

00:50:48.690 --> 00:50:50.700
to mislead his interrogators.

00:50:50.700 --> 00:50:52.170
Bush and his allies knew this,

00:50:52.170 --> 00:50:55.230
it was clearly documented
back in February of 2002,

00:50:55.230 --> 00:50:56.670
and yet publicly,

00:50:56.670 --> 00:50:59.460
the scary story about
Al-Qaeda being in Iraq

00:50:59.460 --> 00:51:02.220
continued to be sold
by Bush and his people.

00:51:02.220 --> 00:51:05.190
- The Iraqi regime has
plotted to develop anthrax,

00:51:05.190 --> 00:51:08.070
nerve gas, and nuclear
weapons for over a decade.

00:51:08.070 --> 00:51:10.380
- [Johnny] The case for weapons
of mass destruction in Iraq

00:51:10.380 --> 00:51:13.560
was equally thin and
senior officials knew it.

00:51:13.560 --> 00:51:15.000
Like in September, 2002,

00:51:15.000 --> 00:51:17.100
when Donald Rumsfeld received this report

00:51:17.100 --> 00:51:18.270
from the Joint Chiefs

00:51:18.270 --> 00:51:20.910
assessing what real
evidence there actually was

00:51:20.910 --> 00:51:22.500
for WMD in Iraq.

00:51:22.500 --> 00:51:24.630
The report is shockingly honest

00:51:24.630 --> 00:51:28.117
and it says that the conclusion
that Saddam has WMD, quote,

00:51:28.117 --> 00:51:31.650
"Relied heavily on analytic
assumptions and judgments

00:51:31.650 --> 00:51:33.480
rather than hard evidence."

00:51:33.480 --> 00:51:37.110
That's word salad for it was
speculation and conjecture.

00:51:37.110 --> 00:51:38.190
The report goes on to say

00:51:38.190 --> 00:51:39.480
that they didn't have anything solid

00:51:39.480 --> 00:51:41.730
on nuclear weapons-related facilities,

00:51:41.730 --> 00:51:43.980
and concludes that they
don't know of any facilities

00:51:43.980 --> 00:51:47.820
where Saddam may be producing
or testing biological weapons.

00:51:47.820 --> 00:51:50.670
And so, we know now that
they had almost no evidence

00:51:50.670 --> 00:51:54.330
for their story about why
the U.S. should invade Iraq.

00:51:54.330 --> 00:51:56.070
And yet even knowing this,

00:51:56.070 --> 00:51:58.440
they kept selling the same story,

00:51:58.440 --> 00:52:00.180
convincing the American people.

00:52:00.180 --> 00:52:01.410
- There's no doubt in my mind

00:52:01.410 --> 00:52:03.060
he wants to have a nuclear weapon

00:52:03.060 --> 00:52:04.830
and he's got some capacity.

00:52:04.830 --> 00:52:07.200
- Wherever threats are
forming against our country,

00:52:07.200 --> 00:52:08.340
we will respond.

00:52:08.340 --> 00:52:10.050
- [Johnny] But they couldn't
go on like this forever.

00:52:10.050 --> 00:52:12.363
They knew that if they were
really gonna sell this war,

00:52:12.363 --> 00:52:15.450
they were going to need to
show real convincing evidence,

00:52:15.450 --> 00:52:18.123
not to the people, but to Congress.

00:52:19.110 --> 00:52:20.850
And this is where we get another instance

00:52:20.850 --> 00:52:24.060
of fixing the intelligence
to fit the policy.

00:52:24.060 --> 00:52:25.710
It came in September, 2002,

00:52:25.710 --> 00:52:27.570
when President Bush asked Congress

00:52:27.570 --> 00:52:29.940
to give him the authority to invade Iraq.

00:52:29.940 --> 00:52:32.370
In response, Senate leaders requested

00:52:32.370 --> 00:52:34.830
an immediate National
Intelligence Estimate,

00:52:34.830 --> 00:52:37.650
which is a report from the
entire intelligence community

00:52:37.650 --> 00:52:40.500
meant to help Congress
make informed decisions.

00:52:40.500 --> 00:52:43.350
This could be really bad
for Bush and his allies.

00:52:43.350 --> 00:52:45.240
So he and the CIA get hard at work

00:52:45.240 --> 00:52:48.000
pulling together a report
that fits their story,

00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:49.230
intelligence to back up

00:52:49.230 --> 00:52:51.570
all their public statements and speeches.

00:52:51.570 --> 00:52:53.970
They come out with this
highly redacted report

00:52:53.970 --> 00:52:56.550
that they deliver in October of 2002.

00:52:56.550 --> 00:52:59.250
The report makes some very strong claims.

00:52:59.250 --> 00:53:02.280
They claim that Iraq has
been building more WMD,

00:53:02.280 --> 00:53:04.860
that they have chemical
and biological weapons,

00:53:04.860 --> 00:53:08.790
and that they will have a nuclear
weapon during this decade.

00:53:08.790 --> 00:53:11.550
And to congressional leaders,
this appeared rock solid.

00:53:11.550 --> 00:53:13.440
Here was the entire intelligence community

00:53:13.440 --> 00:53:17.040
coming together saying that
Iraq had horrific weapons

00:53:17.040 --> 00:53:18.570
and that they wanted to get more.

00:53:18.570 --> 00:53:22.890
- Saddam Hussein has composed
a scarlet chapter of terror.

00:53:22.890 --> 00:53:25.110
Our only responsible option

00:53:25.110 --> 00:53:28.290
is to confront this threat
before Americans die.

00:53:28.290 --> 00:53:31.410
- There is no such thing as
a Democrat or Republican war.

00:53:31.410 --> 00:53:32.340
- [Johnny] So in that same month,

00:53:32.340 --> 00:53:34.980
based on this report and all
of these public speeches,

00:53:34.980 --> 00:53:37.268
Congress gives the green light for war.

00:53:37.268 --> 00:53:41.520
(heart beat thumping)
(distressing music)

00:53:41.520 --> 00:53:44.880
But this National Intelligence
Estimate was deeply flawed.

00:53:44.880 --> 00:53:47.520
It was a perfect example
of the fixed intelligence

00:53:47.520 --> 00:53:49.470
described in the Downing Street memo.

00:53:49.470 --> 00:53:52.620
It was put together in less
than a month, totally rushed.

00:53:52.620 --> 00:53:54.990
The report had been plagued by groupthink

00:53:54.990 --> 00:53:57.300
and directed by political pressure

00:53:57.300 --> 00:53:59.400
with the Bush administration
pushing analysts

00:53:59.400 --> 00:54:02.160
to deliver a report that
matched their conclusions

00:54:02.160 --> 00:54:04.560
that they had already
come to months earlier.

00:54:04.560 --> 00:54:07.980
And they did this using
very old intelligence.

00:54:07.980 --> 00:54:11.190
The CIA hadn't had any human
assets on the ground for years,

00:54:11.190 --> 00:54:12.030
so their report

00:54:12.030 --> 00:54:15.420
wasn't even based off
of anything after 1998.

00:54:15.420 --> 00:54:16.500
But it didn't matter,

00:54:16.500 --> 00:54:18.960
Bush and his allies had
successfully sold the war

00:54:18.960 --> 00:54:21.330
to Congress and the American people.

00:54:21.330 --> 00:54:23.130
But there was one last hurdle.

00:54:23.130 --> 00:54:24.870
It was the international community,

00:54:24.870 --> 00:54:27.750
which would mean they would
have to face the UN process

00:54:27.750 --> 00:54:30.840
that they apparently had no patience for.

00:54:30.840 --> 00:54:33.690
- Iraq has answered a decade of UN demands

00:54:33.690 --> 00:54:35.760
with a decade of defiance.

00:54:35.760 --> 00:54:37.470
- [Johnny] So it's November, 2002,

00:54:37.470 --> 00:54:39.600
and in response to the rising tensions

00:54:39.600 --> 00:54:41.460
between Iraq and the U.S.,

00:54:41.460 --> 00:54:45.780
the UN Security Council
passes this resolution, 1441.

00:54:45.780 --> 00:54:47.760
It was a measure that
was meant to give Iraq

00:54:47.760 --> 00:54:51.390
a final opportunity to comply
with weapons inspections

00:54:51.390 --> 00:54:53.850
to show the world that
they had fully disarmed

00:54:53.850 --> 00:54:55.980
and had no weapons of mass destruction.

00:54:55.980 --> 00:54:58.650
Bush and his allies saw
this as an opportunity,

00:54:58.650 --> 00:54:59.910
if they could somehow show

00:54:59.910 --> 00:55:03.600
that Iraq wasn't complying with
this new inspection process,

00:55:03.600 --> 00:55:05.130
this resolution implied

00:55:05.130 --> 00:55:07.890
that they would be justified
in invading the country.

00:55:07.890 --> 00:55:10.740
Their long-desired war would be on.

00:55:10.740 --> 00:55:11.940
But they had a problem,

00:55:11.940 --> 00:55:14.010
which is that Iraq and Saddam Hussein

00:55:14.010 --> 00:55:16.650
were complying with the
weapons inspections.

00:55:16.650 --> 00:55:18.000
Over the course of four months,

00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:21.840
UN weapons inspectors searched
Iraq from top to bottom.

00:55:21.840 --> 00:55:23.490
They were led by Hans Blix,

00:55:23.490 --> 00:55:26.070
the former Head of the
International Atomic Energy Agency.

00:55:26.070 --> 00:55:31.070
They conducted over 900
inspections at over 500 locations

00:55:31.200 --> 00:55:32.790
and they didn't find anything,

00:55:32.790 --> 00:55:37.790
no WMD, no biological weapons,
no nuclear weapons programs.

00:55:37.890 --> 00:55:40.260
- Iraq has, on the whole,
cooperated rather well.

00:55:40.260 --> 00:55:41.790
Access has been provided

00:55:41.790 --> 00:55:43.920
to all sites we have wanted to inspect,

00:55:43.920 --> 00:55:45.630
universities, military bases,

00:55:45.630 --> 00:55:48.120
presidential sites,
and private residences.

00:55:48.120 --> 00:55:49.950
- [Johnny] Hans Blix did find two things

00:55:49.950 --> 00:55:51.180
that were important.

00:55:51.180 --> 00:55:53.460
First, they did find
some ballistic missiles

00:55:53.460 --> 00:55:55.500
that the UN says have an effective range

00:55:55.500 --> 00:55:56.790
that makes them illegal,

00:55:56.790 --> 00:55:58.920
so they would need to
be destroyed by Iraq.

00:55:58.920 --> 00:56:01.140
And second, there were
some chemical weapons

00:56:01.140 --> 00:56:04.470
that the Iraqi regime said
cannot be accounted for.

00:56:04.470 --> 00:56:06.690
But Blix insists that this does not mean

00:56:06.690 --> 00:56:08.400
that they have these weapons,

00:56:08.400 --> 00:56:10.110
it just means that they need more time

00:56:10.110 --> 00:56:12.240
to work out the accounting situation.

00:56:12.240 --> 00:56:15.030
But this error was exactly
what the Bush circle needed

00:56:15.030 --> 00:56:16.680
to justify their invasion.

00:56:16.680 --> 00:56:17.513
- [UN Announcer] I call now

00:56:17.513 --> 00:56:20.100
on the distinguished Secretary of State

00:56:20.100 --> 00:56:21.870
of the United States of America.

00:56:21.870 --> 00:56:24.030
- [Johnny] They sent their
most respected cabinet member

00:56:24.030 --> 00:56:26.820
to the UN, Secretary
of State, Colin Powell.

00:56:26.820 --> 00:56:28.500
He came equipped with photos

00:56:28.500 --> 00:56:31.890
of what he says are
mobile weapons facilities.

00:56:31.890 --> 00:56:35.400
- Saddam Hussein and his regime
are concealing their efforts

00:56:35.400 --> 00:56:38.280
to produce more weapons
of mass destruction.

00:56:38.280 --> 00:56:40.560
- [Johnny] He plays
tapes that he says prove

00:56:40.560 --> 00:56:43.020
that the Iraqis are hiding their weapons.

00:56:43.020 --> 00:56:45.120
- [Powell] We evacuated
everything to make sure

00:56:45.120 --> 00:56:48.000
it was not around when
the inspectors showed up.

00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:50.400
- [Johnny] And then he says
that this is solid evidence

00:56:50.400 --> 00:56:53.280
that shows that Iraq is
violating the UN resolution

00:56:53.280 --> 00:56:54.660
that told them to disarm.

00:56:54.660 --> 00:56:57.480
This whole thing contradicts
what the UN weapons inspectors

00:56:57.480 --> 00:57:00.600
had found in their hundreds
and hundreds of inspections.

00:57:00.600 --> 00:57:01.770
They bulldozed the process,

00:57:01.770 --> 00:57:04.080
and say they have justification to invade.

00:57:04.080 --> 00:57:05.700
- My colleagues, we have an obligation

00:57:05.700 --> 00:57:09.390
to see that our resolutions
are complied with.

00:57:09.390 --> 00:57:11.340
- They've got the
American public on board,

00:57:11.340 --> 00:57:12.810
they've got Congress on board,

00:57:12.810 --> 00:57:15.003
and now the UK is in lockstep.

00:57:16.024 --> 00:57:17.490
- This is the time for this house

00:57:17.490 --> 00:57:20.730
to show that we will stand up
for what we know to be right,

00:57:20.730 --> 00:57:22.320
to show that we will confront

00:57:22.320 --> 00:57:24.630
the tyrannies and
dictatorships and terrorists

00:57:24.630 --> 00:57:26.700
who put our way of life at risk.

00:57:26.700 --> 00:57:29.580
- [Johnny] The Bush administration
abandons the UN process,

00:57:29.580 --> 00:57:31.320
and that March, his people do

00:57:31.320 --> 00:57:33.630
what they set out to do 18 months earlier,

00:57:33.630 --> 00:57:36.109
when they were looking
for something else to bomb

00:57:36.109 --> 00:57:37.620
(missile roars)

00:57:37.620 --> 00:57:40.650
to show who's really in
charge on the world stage.

00:57:40.650 --> 00:57:41.820
- My fellow citizens,

00:57:41.820 --> 00:57:44.700
American and coalition forces
are in the early stages

00:57:44.700 --> 00:57:48.270
of military operations to
disarm Iraq, to free its people,

00:57:48.270 --> 00:57:50.370
and to defend the world from grave danger.

00:57:50.370 --> 00:57:53.280
America faces an enemy that has no regard

00:57:53.280 --> 00:57:56.586
for conventions of war
or rules of morality.

00:57:56.586 --> 00:57:58.878
(tense music)

00:57:58.878 --> 00:58:01.878
(explosion booming)

00:58:07.947 --> 00:58:10.530
(gunshots pop)

00:58:12.240 --> 00:58:13.950
- [Johnny] Bush's war took the life

00:58:13.950 --> 00:58:16.680
of an estimated half million Iraqis,

00:58:16.680 --> 00:58:19.440
and thousands more who
fought for their country.

00:58:19.440 --> 00:58:22.260
And over the course of
a decade occupying Iraq,

00:58:22.260 --> 00:58:25.140
no weapons were found,
no nuclear facilities,

00:58:25.140 --> 00:58:27.120
no mobile weapons labs.

00:58:27.120 --> 00:58:28.920
In fact, it seemed like Iraq

00:58:28.920 --> 00:58:32.340
had dismantled its nuclear
program back in 1991,

00:58:32.340 --> 00:58:34.620
and the rest of its chemical
and biological weapons

00:58:34.620 --> 00:58:35.853
just a few years later.

00:58:37.290 --> 00:58:38.340
After the invasion,

00:58:38.340 --> 00:58:40.260
the U.S. never allowed the UN inspectors

00:58:40.260 --> 00:58:43.020
back into the country to
help with their search.

00:58:43.020 --> 00:58:44.400
The U.S. would never find a way

00:58:44.400 --> 00:58:48.540
to link the Iraqi regime
to Al-Qaeda or to anthrax.

00:58:48.540 --> 00:58:50.490
Colin Powell, the Secretary of State,

00:58:50.490 --> 00:58:52.830
who played a major role
in selling this war

00:58:52.830 --> 00:58:54.720
to the international community

00:58:54.720 --> 00:58:56.970
would later say that he regrets his part

00:58:56.970 --> 00:58:57.990
in starting the war.

00:58:57.990 --> 00:59:00.960
- I deeply regret that some
of the information I presented

00:59:00.960 --> 00:59:02.700
which was multi-source was wrong.

00:59:02.700 --> 00:59:04.620
- [Johnny] Hans Blix, the
Chief Weapons Inspector

00:59:04.620 --> 00:59:06.720
for the UN, would comment later that year

00:59:06.720 --> 00:59:08.550
that, "It is sort of fascinating

00:59:08.550 --> 00:59:10.710
that you can have 100% certainty

00:59:10.710 --> 00:59:12.720
about weapons of mass destruction

00:59:12.720 --> 00:59:15.117
and zero certainty about where they are."

00:59:16.650 --> 00:59:18.660
We may never know what was in the heart

00:59:18.660 --> 00:59:20.730
and minds of these senior leaders,

00:59:20.730 --> 00:59:23.340
whether they truly
believed their own lies,

00:59:23.340 --> 00:59:26.250
whether they felt justified
in the choices they made.

00:59:26.250 --> 00:59:28.230
But what we can learn from this story

00:59:28.230 --> 00:59:30.000
is how these leaders behaved

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:31.980
when they thought no one was watching,

00:59:31.980 --> 00:59:33.060
when they thought they could tell

00:59:33.060 --> 00:59:35.040
a compelling story to the public

00:59:35.040 --> 00:59:37.860
while having a totally
different set of motivations.

00:59:37.860 --> 00:59:41.190
And how, with enough fear
and enough deception,

00:59:41.190 --> 00:59:45.540
you can lead an entire society
into an unprovoked war,

00:59:45.540 --> 00:59:48.033
changing the course of
history in the process.

00:59:51.889 --> 00:59:53.100
(subdued music)

00:59:53.100 --> 00:59:55.200
Up in the Zagros Mountains

00:59:55.200 --> 00:59:57.487
have long lived a people called the Kurds.

00:59:57.487 --> 01:00:00.270
They're a people with a
centuries long history

01:00:00.270 --> 01:00:02.220
of fighting back against invaders

01:00:02.220 --> 01:00:05.340
who have crossed through their
lands, resisting conquest

01:00:05.340 --> 01:00:08.310
in the name of defending their
shared cultural identity.

01:00:08.310 --> 01:00:10.020
Some living as nomads,

01:00:10.020 --> 01:00:13.173
a people with no friends
but these mountains.

01:00:14.970 --> 01:00:16.200
Eventually the Ottoman Empire

01:00:16.200 --> 01:00:19.560
did take over all of this
territory, but even then,

01:00:19.560 --> 01:00:21.960
the Kurds maintained
large amounts of autonomy

01:00:21.960 --> 01:00:23.760
and freedom in their land.

01:00:23.760 --> 01:00:25.440
Then came World War I

01:00:25.440 --> 01:00:28.620
when the European powers
defeated the Ottoman Empire

01:00:28.620 --> 01:00:30.303
and conquered all of this.

01:00:32.580 --> 01:00:33.600
The winners got together

01:00:33.600 --> 01:00:36.570
and discussed how they would
carve it up between them.

01:00:36.570 --> 01:00:38.640
If you look back at old European maps,

01:00:38.640 --> 01:00:42.360
you'll see that all of this
area would be labeled Kurdistan,

01:00:42.360 --> 01:00:44.340
an area where the Kurdish people lived

01:00:44.340 --> 01:00:46.590
and had some self-rule.

01:00:46.590 --> 01:00:48.150
So while drawing these lines,

01:00:48.150 --> 01:00:52.110
the British wanted to mark all
of this as Kurdish territory,

01:00:52.110 --> 01:00:54.810
paving away for an independent
country for the Kurds,

01:00:54.810 --> 01:00:57.450
but the new leader of
Turkey opposed this plan.

01:00:57.450 --> 01:00:58.740
He didn't wanna give all this land

01:00:58.740 --> 01:01:01.020
and resources to the Kurds.

01:01:01.020 --> 01:01:03.663
So he pushed the European
forces out of Turkey.

01:01:05.160 --> 01:01:08.610
They gave up on this plan to
give the Kurds their own land.

01:01:08.610 --> 01:01:12.363
And in the end, instead of
drawing borders around the Kurds,

01:01:13.230 --> 01:01:15.693
the Europeans drew borders through them.

01:01:21.060 --> 01:01:23.010
What could have been Kurdistan

01:01:23.010 --> 01:01:25.740
was now five different territories,

01:01:25.740 --> 01:01:27.386
the Kurds split between them.

01:01:27.386 --> 01:01:28.219
(inquisitive music)

01:01:28.219 --> 01:01:30.450
But at first these were
just lines on a map

01:01:30.450 --> 01:01:33.420
and the Kurds continued to
move through this region.

01:01:33.420 --> 01:01:35.070
Eventually the Europeans left,

01:01:35.070 --> 01:01:37.140
and these became independent countries

01:01:37.140 --> 01:01:40.950
with leaders who wanted to
consolidate and centralize power.

01:01:40.950 --> 01:01:43.980
So these lines hardened,
restricting the Kurds' movement

01:01:43.980 --> 01:01:45.870
and their livelihood in this region.

01:01:45.870 --> 01:01:48.360
But even still, across this region,

01:01:48.360 --> 01:01:50.220
the Kurds didn't give up on their idea

01:01:50.220 --> 01:01:53.760
of someday gaining
independence, self-rule,

01:01:53.760 --> 01:01:55.622
or maybe even a country of their own.

01:01:55.622 --> 01:01:58.539
(foreboding music)

01:02:00.810 --> 01:02:02.040
Throughout the 1900s,

01:02:02.040 --> 01:02:03.660
the Kurds in each of these new countries

01:02:03.660 --> 01:02:04.860
took different approaches

01:02:04.860 --> 01:02:07.380
to fight for an independent Kurdish state.

01:02:07.380 --> 01:02:11.790
Some Kurds would use politics,
others would use violence.

01:02:11.790 --> 01:02:14.250
The early uprisings were
crushed by the leaders

01:02:14.250 --> 01:02:17.400
of these new countries who
saw the Kurds as a threat

01:02:17.400 --> 01:02:19.560
to their efforts to unify their country

01:02:19.560 --> 01:02:21.483
around a common language and culture.

01:02:22.620 --> 01:02:26.370
Like in Iran, where the Kurds
had some political rights,

01:02:26.370 --> 01:02:27.660
but they fought for more.

01:02:27.660 --> 01:02:29.820
They wanted autonomy and independence.

01:02:29.820 --> 01:02:31.920
The government of Iran
wouldn't have any of this.

01:02:31.920 --> 01:02:34.380
They would crack down with
violence on the Kurds,

01:02:34.380 --> 01:02:36.600
often supported by Western powers.

01:02:36.600 --> 01:02:39.450
By the 1970s, Iran was
going through a revolution

01:02:39.450 --> 01:02:41.850
and the Kurds tried again to rise up,

01:02:41.850 --> 01:02:44.190
but this new regime had no tolerance

01:02:44.190 --> 01:02:46.530
for a group that would
challenge the leadership

01:02:46.530 --> 01:02:48.273
of the ruling religious leader.

01:02:49.110 --> 01:02:51.513
So once again, they were put down.

01:02:54.390 --> 01:02:57.180
Over in Iraq, Kurdish fighters fought hard

01:02:57.180 --> 01:02:59.730
against the government
throughout the 20th century,

01:02:59.730 --> 01:03:03.240
until the 1970s, when
this new regime came in

01:03:03.240 --> 01:03:05.370
and made a deal with the Kurds,

01:03:05.370 --> 01:03:08.070
saying that they would be
recognized as an ethnic group

01:03:08.070 --> 01:03:10.800
and would be guaranteed
political representation.

01:03:10.800 --> 01:03:12.840
It seemed like a huge deal for the Kurds,

01:03:12.840 --> 01:03:15.360
but it turned out to be a false promise.

01:03:15.360 --> 01:03:18.090
The Iraqi regime, now
led by Saddam Hussein,

01:03:18.090 --> 01:03:20.340
would continue to repress the Kurds,

01:03:20.340 --> 01:03:22.530
eventually dropping
deadly chemical weapons

01:03:22.530 --> 01:03:24.240
on Kurdish towns in Iraq,

01:03:24.240 --> 01:03:27.150
systematically killing
thousands of Kurdish civilians

01:03:27.150 --> 01:03:29.880
in a genocide supported
by American-made supplies

01:03:29.880 --> 01:03:31.383
that were sold to Saddam.

01:03:33.870 --> 01:03:36.480
Over in Syria, the Kurds
were treated decently

01:03:36.480 --> 01:03:38.464
under the French-controlled government.

01:03:38.464 --> 01:03:39.420
(subdued music)

01:03:39.420 --> 01:03:41.883
They were citizens and had some rights.

01:03:43.590 --> 01:03:45.570
But after the French left in the 40s,

01:03:45.570 --> 01:03:48.750
the regimes that came
after oppressed the Kurds,

01:03:48.750 --> 01:03:50.160
and by the 1970s,

01:03:50.160 --> 01:03:53.250
the Syrian government was
arresting and deporting them,

01:03:53.250 --> 01:03:56.070
taking their land and giving it to Arabs.

01:03:56.070 --> 01:03:57.990
In total, the Syrian government

01:03:57.990 --> 01:04:02.400
would remove 140,000
Kurds from the country.

01:04:02.400 --> 01:04:05.070
Decades later, Syria and the United States

01:04:05.070 --> 01:04:07.860
would both find the Kurds in Syria useful

01:04:07.860 --> 01:04:09.543
for their political goals.

01:04:11.880 --> 01:04:13.599
But first, let's talk about Turkey.

01:04:13.599 --> 01:04:14.970
(inquisitive music)

01:04:14.970 --> 01:04:18.270
There's more Kurdish people
here than in any other country.

01:04:18.270 --> 01:04:19.140
The same government

01:04:19.140 --> 01:04:22.320
that had fought against
a Kurdish state early on

01:04:22.320 --> 01:04:24.390
continued to oppress the Kurds,

01:04:24.390 --> 01:04:27.480
denying them citizenship,
outlawing their language,

01:04:27.480 --> 01:04:29.370
and keeping them out of politics,

01:04:29.370 --> 01:04:32.550
all with the goal of wiping
out their culture from Turkey

01:04:32.550 --> 01:04:35.310
as a part of this Turkification campaign,

01:04:35.310 --> 01:04:38.760
which tried to unify
Turkey under one culture,

01:04:38.760 --> 01:04:41.640
targeting the Kurds and
other ethnic minorities.

01:04:41.640 --> 01:04:44.700
Some Kurds fought back against
this in the early years,

01:04:44.700 --> 01:04:46.665
but were quickly crushed
by the Turkish state,

01:04:46.665 --> 01:04:48.330
(explosions boom)

01:04:48.330 --> 01:04:51.030
leading to the creation of
an armed insurgent group

01:04:51.030 --> 01:04:52.860
with communist ideology.

01:04:52.860 --> 01:04:55.677
They're called the Kurdish
Workers Party, or PKK,

01:04:55.677 --> 01:04:56.850
and it would become one of

01:04:56.850 --> 01:04:59.130
the biggest Turkish resistance movements.

01:04:59.130 --> 01:05:02.880
The PKK would use violence
like suicide bombings

01:05:02.880 --> 01:05:04.770
and improvised explosives,

01:05:04.770 --> 01:05:06.570
as well as youth militia fighters

01:05:06.570 --> 01:05:08.310
against the Turkish government,

01:05:08.310 --> 01:05:10.230
tactics that they say are the only way

01:05:10.230 --> 01:05:12.600
to fight back against such oppression.

01:05:12.600 --> 01:05:15.660
And as a result, Turkey
and most Western powers

01:05:15.660 --> 01:05:18.093
consider the PKK a terrorist group.

01:05:20.340 --> 01:05:22.950
So that's how the Kurds
in these four countries

01:05:22.950 --> 01:05:26.370
became locked in a conflict
with their governments.

01:05:26.370 --> 01:05:28.230
They all have different struggles,

01:05:28.230 --> 01:05:30.180
but they're all unified by the dream

01:05:30.180 --> 01:05:32.765
of some version of Kurdish independence.

01:05:32.765 --> 01:05:34.080
(subdued music)

01:05:34.080 --> 01:05:36.330
But it doesn't take long for these regimes

01:05:36.330 --> 01:05:40.203
to see that they could use the
Kurds as a tool, as a weapon.

01:05:41.100 --> 01:05:42.750
One of the earliest examples of this

01:05:42.750 --> 01:05:44.820
happens at the end of World War II

01:05:44.820 --> 01:05:48.090
when the Soviet Union sees
an opportunity to gain land

01:05:48.090 --> 01:05:52.410
and access to oil by supplying
and arming the Kurds in Iran,

01:05:52.410 --> 01:05:54.870
allowing them to rise up
against the government

01:05:54.870 --> 01:05:59.070
and declare their own country
supported by the Soviet Union.

01:05:59.070 --> 01:06:00.450
But it didn't work.

01:06:00.450 --> 01:06:02.820
The U.S. pressures the Soviets to leave,

01:06:02.820 --> 01:06:05.550
and now without support,
the government of Iran,

01:06:05.550 --> 01:06:07.710
which is backed by the U.S. and UK,

01:06:07.710 --> 01:06:11.550
go on to crush this movement
of Kurds in their country.

01:06:11.550 --> 01:06:14.433
The Kurds are back to being
repressed by the government.

01:06:16.920 --> 01:06:19.650
In the 1980s, Syria uses the Kurds

01:06:19.650 --> 01:06:22.050
as a weapon against its rival Turkey

01:06:22.050 --> 01:06:26.520
when it allows the PKK to
start operating within Syria,

01:06:26.520 --> 01:06:30.063
giving them money and weapons
so that they can hurt Turkey.

01:06:31.830 --> 01:06:35.190
Syria is doing this in
spite of having spent years

01:06:35.190 --> 01:06:37.500
removing hundreds of thousands of Kurds

01:06:37.500 --> 01:06:38.733
from its own country.

01:06:41.280 --> 01:06:43.920
This escalates the
conflict between these two,

01:06:43.920 --> 01:06:46.803
and Turkey threatens to invade Syria.

01:06:48.030 --> 01:06:51.360
So Syria backs down and kicks the PKK out

01:06:51.360 --> 01:06:53.250
to avoid being invaded,

01:06:53.250 --> 01:06:55.890
showing once again how the
Kurds' willingness to fight

01:06:55.890 --> 01:07:00.300
can easily become a pawn in
the geopolitics of the region,

01:07:00.300 --> 01:07:02.643
discarded once they aren't useful anymore.

01:07:03.502 --> 01:07:06.840
In the 1980s, Iran and
Iraq both used the Kurds

01:07:06.840 --> 01:07:10.080
at the same time as a
weapon to hurt each other,

01:07:10.080 --> 01:07:12.840
even as both are cracking down on Kurds

01:07:12.840 --> 01:07:14.250
in their own country.

01:07:14.250 --> 01:07:17.910
Saddam Hussein funds and
arms the Kurds in Iran,

01:07:17.910 --> 01:07:21.510
while Iran funds the
Kurds in northern Iraq,

01:07:21.510 --> 01:07:24.090
both sides hoping to
spark a Kurdish uprising

01:07:24.090 --> 01:07:26.820
that will distract and weaken their enemy.

01:07:26.820 --> 01:07:29.130
In Iraq, Saddam Hussein retaliates

01:07:29.130 --> 01:07:30.930
against the Kurds in his country

01:07:30.930 --> 01:07:34.020
with that genocidal chemical
attack we talked about earlier

01:07:34.020 --> 01:07:36.630
that killed at least 50,000 Kurdish people

01:07:36.630 --> 01:07:38.073
and probably much more.

01:07:39.180 --> 01:07:41.670
Once again, the Kurdish
dream of independence

01:07:41.670 --> 01:07:44.160
was used by outsiders as a weapon,

01:07:44.160 --> 01:07:46.378
and the Kurdish people
paid heavily for it.

01:07:46.378 --> 01:07:47.790
(intense music)

01:07:47.790 --> 01:07:50.640
The U.S. would get
involved when in the '90s

01:07:50.640 --> 01:07:51.900
they would come to this region

01:07:51.900 --> 01:07:55.170
fighting against Saddam
Hussein for the first time.

01:07:55.170 --> 01:07:57.120
The U.S. rallies the Kurds,

01:07:57.120 --> 01:07:59.250
calling for them to overthrow Saddam.

01:07:59.250 --> 01:08:02.250
George Bush Sr. literally
calls them to action

01:08:02.250 --> 01:08:05.670
with television and radio
broadcasts throughout the country.

01:08:05.670 --> 01:08:08.490
- That the Iraqi people
should put him aside,

01:08:08.490 --> 01:08:12.870
and that would facilitate the resolution

01:08:12.870 --> 01:08:14.580
of all these problems that exist

01:08:14.580 --> 01:08:18.180
and certainly would facilitate
the acceptance of Iraq

01:08:18.180 --> 01:08:20.970
back into the family of
peace-loving nations.

01:08:20.970 --> 01:08:22.410
- [Johnny] And it seems to work.

01:08:22.410 --> 01:08:25.980
It sparks an uprising that
looks successful at first.

01:08:25.980 --> 01:08:28.740
The U.S. had instigated this uprising,

01:08:28.740 --> 01:08:30.450
and they have forces in the region

01:08:30.450 --> 01:08:33.210
that they could send to support the Kurds,

01:08:33.210 --> 01:08:34.680
but they do nothing.

01:08:34.680 --> 01:08:37.590
This allows Saddam to regather his forces

01:08:37.590 --> 01:08:41.100
and crush this coup and to
increase this oppression,

01:08:41.100 --> 01:08:43.650
ensuring that nothing like
this ever happens again.

01:08:44.700 --> 01:08:46.950
Now, the U.S. and UK do eventually step in

01:08:46.950 --> 01:08:48.930
to create this no-fly zone

01:08:48.930 --> 01:08:50.670
meant to protect the Kurds in the north

01:08:50.670 --> 01:08:52.230
and the Shiites in the south.

01:08:52.230 --> 01:08:55.170
This gives the Kurds some
autonomy over their region

01:08:55.170 --> 01:08:58.473
and protects them from further
airstrikes by the Iraqi Army.

01:08:59.490 --> 01:09:01.830
Soon the U.S. is back in Iraq.

01:09:01.830 --> 01:09:05.610
It's 2003, and the Bush
administration decides to invade

01:09:05.610 --> 01:09:07.530
and remove Saddam from power.

01:09:07.530 --> 01:09:11.070
The Kurds in Iraq hope that the
U.S. presence in this region

01:09:11.070 --> 01:09:14.190
will mean finally they
will get their own state,

01:09:14.190 --> 01:09:15.900
they will be independent.

01:09:15.900 --> 01:09:18.540
They join the U.S. in
fighting against Saddam

01:09:18.540 --> 01:09:21.180
and his loyalists, battling insurgents,

01:09:21.180 --> 01:09:22.499
and later against ISIS.

01:09:22.499 --> 01:09:25.230
(gunshots crackle)

01:09:25.230 --> 01:09:27.600
The Kurds would even go on to hold a vote,

01:09:27.600 --> 01:09:30.060
showing that 92% of the population

01:09:30.060 --> 01:09:32.550
was in favor of independence,

01:09:32.550 --> 01:09:34.740
but the U.S. won't support this,

01:09:34.740 --> 01:09:38.220
worried that it might
destabilize this new Iraqi state

01:09:38.220 --> 01:09:40.620
that the U.S. just propped up.

01:09:40.620 --> 01:09:41.910
Even when the Kurds fight

01:09:41.910 --> 01:09:44.520
on the side of the U.S.
and their interests,

01:09:44.520 --> 01:09:48.510
U.S. support for their cause
still remains very limited.

01:09:48.510 --> 01:09:49.860
They still look the other way

01:09:49.860 --> 01:09:54.003
as Turkey bombs their towns
in Iraq hunting for the PKK.

01:09:55.800 --> 01:09:58.590
This same pattern has
continued in recent years

01:09:58.590 --> 01:10:00.210
in the country of Syria,

01:10:00.210 --> 01:10:03.870
a country that descended
into civil war around 2011.

01:10:03.870 --> 01:10:05.610
This chaos looked like an opportunity

01:10:05.610 --> 01:10:09.510
for the Kurds in Syria, a
chance to establish real control

01:10:09.510 --> 01:10:12.090
over what they see as a part of Kurdistan.

01:10:12.090 --> 01:10:15.780
The PKK in Turkey helps
create a new Kurdish militia

01:10:15.780 --> 01:10:20.130
called the People's
Protection Unit or YPG.

01:10:20.130 --> 01:10:22.680
They seize large swaths
of land in the north

01:10:22.680 --> 01:10:24.870
and they declare self-governance.

01:10:24.870 --> 01:10:27.150
Around this same time,
the terrorist group ISIS

01:10:27.150 --> 01:10:29.160
is taking huge swaths of territory

01:10:29.160 --> 01:10:31.260
in the north and east of the country,

01:10:31.260 --> 01:10:33.303
creating their so-called caliphate.

01:10:34.890 --> 01:10:37.110
And here comes the U.S. once again

01:10:37.110 --> 01:10:39.030
asking the Kurds for help,

01:10:39.030 --> 01:10:40.980
hoping that they will fight against ISIS

01:10:40.980 --> 01:10:42.240
on the ground for them.

01:10:42.240 --> 01:10:46.560
But because this group
is allied with the PKK,

01:10:46.560 --> 01:10:48.510
which they consider a terrorist group,

01:10:48.510 --> 01:10:51.630
the U.S. asks this militia
to rebrand themselves

01:10:51.630 --> 01:10:53.730
to the Syrian Democratic Forces,

01:10:53.730 --> 01:10:56.490
which obscures their
connection to the PKK.

01:10:56.490 --> 01:11:00.450
The U.S. then trains, funds,
and arms them to fight ISIS.

01:11:00.450 --> 01:11:04.140
The Kurds are, once
again, the U.S.'s weapon.

01:11:04.140 --> 01:11:07.590
This plan works, and with
help from U.S. airstrikes,

01:11:07.590 --> 01:11:11.520
this Kurdish militia kicks
ISIS out of more and more land.

01:11:11.520 --> 01:11:13.140
But Turkey hates this.

01:11:13.140 --> 01:11:15.540
All they see is a potential Kurdish state

01:11:15.540 --> 01:11:19.380
right on their southern border,
a safe haven for the PKK

01:11:19.380 --> 01:11:22.320
that will allow more attacks
against the Turkish military.

01:11:22.320 --> 01:11:24.840
But Turkey can't attack
this branch of the Kurds

01:11:24.840 --> 01:11:27.390
while they're being supported
by the United States.

01:11:27.390 --> 01:11:30.360
Lucky for them, there's a new
president in the White House

01:11:30.360 --> 01:11:33.870
and he's promised to pull the
U.S. out of the war in Syria.

01:11:33.870 --> 01:11:36.810
And in 2019, to the dismay of the Kurds,

01:11:36.810 --> 01:11:38.490
he makes good on this promise.

01:11:38.490 --> 01:11:41.580
With the U.S. out of
the way, Turkey invades,

01:11:41.580 --> 01:11:43.380
launching airstrikes and artillery

01:11:43.380 --> 01:11:45.630
against the Kurds in this border region,

01:11:45.630 --> 01:11:47.070
saying that their plan is to create

01:11:47.070 --> 01:11:51.060
a 32-kilometer-deep safe zone
right here along the border,

01:11:51.060 --> 01:11:53.520
and that no Kurdish forces
are allowed to be here.

01:11:53.520 --> 01:11:56.460
The plan was to then
resettle Syrian refugees

01:11:56.460 --> 01:11:58.173
currently living in Turkey.

01:11:59.850 --> 01:12:01.080
It's a brutal campaign

01:12:01.080 --> 01:12:03.180
that looks a lot like what Syria was doing

01:12:03.180 --> 01:12:04.743
to the Kurds in the '70s.

01:12:06.713 --> 01:12:08.910
(missile whooshes)

01:12:08.910 --> 01:12:11.520
The U.S. completely abandons the Kurds,

01:12:11.520 --> 01:12:14.580
even after using them to
fight their enemy ISIS.

01:12:14.580 --> 01:12:18.870
Turkey, a NATO and U.S.
ally, continues to bomb them

01:12:18.870 --> 01:12:21.360
using weapons from the United States.

01:12:21.360 --> 01:12:24.270
They spend the next four
years sending drone strikes

01:12:24.270 --> 01:12:26.700
and airstrikes into Syria and Iraq,

01:12:26.700 --> 01:12:29.083
anywhere they think
the PKK has a presence.

01:12:29.083 --> 01:12:29.916
(subdued music)

01:12:29.916 --> 01:12:33.123
This map shows all of their
attacks during this time.

01:12:35.160 --> 01:12:38.553
You can see that it's not just
against the Kurds in Turkey,

01:12:39.630 --> 01:12:41.433
but across this whole region.

01:12:45.150 --> 01:12:47.550
Today, the Kurdish groups in this region

01:12:47.550 --> 01:12:51.300
vary more widely than ever,
each with different values

01:12:51.300 --> 01:12:53.130
and visions for the future,

01:12:53.130 --> 01:12:57.000
forged from each of their
unique struggles and traumas.

01:12:57.000 --> 01:12:59.580
Kurdish groups still fight
the government in Iran

01:12:59.580 --> 01:13:01.620
with the goal of creating their own state.

01:13:01.620 --> 01:13:04.667
The Kurds in Iraq did gain
some autonomy from the U.S.

01:13:04.667 --> 01:13:07.080
in the new Iraqi constitution,

01:13:07.080 --> 01:13:09.750
but it doesn't seem like
this autonomy will last.

01:13:09.750 --> 01:13:13.440
As recently, the Iraqi Army
is fighting with the Kurds

01:13:13.440 --> 01:13:17.310
to maintain control over the
oil resources in this area

01:13:17.310 --> 01:13:19.650
to keep the Kurds economically dependent

01:13:19.650 --> 01:13:22.710
on the central government so
that they never break away.

01:13:22.710 --> 01:13:25.080
Once again, the U.S. is
not supporting the Kurds

01:13:25.080 --> 01:13:25.913
in this fight.

01:13:27.210 --> 01:13:30.780
Turkey continues its
offensive against the PKK

01:13:30.780 --> 01:13:32.757
and other Kurdish groups in the region,

01:13:32.757 --> 01:13:35.490
and they continue to crack
down on the Kurds politically,

01:13:35.490 --> 01:13:38.100
arresting Kurdish
politicians and activists,

01:13:38.100 --> 01:13:41.160
censoring journalists to
intimidate the Kurdish people

01:13:41.160 --> 01:13:43.740
from participating in the election.

01:13:43.740 --> 01:13:47.730
The Kurds in Syria face a
new and uncertain future.

01:13:47.730 --> 01:13:50.490
They do have some autonomy
up here in the north,

01:13:50.490 --> 01:13:52.470
but are surrounded by enemies,

01:13:52.470 --> 01:13:55.623
no longer counting on
any support from the U.S.

01:13:58.650 --> 01:14:01.440
The story of the Kurds
is the story of a people

01:14:01.440 --> 01:14:04.380
who are willing to fight like few others,

01:14:04.380 --> 01:14:07.080
all in the name of their
culture and identity.

01:14:07.080 --> 01:14:09.810
That willingness to fight
has presented a threat

01:14:09.810 --> 01:14:13.650
to regional governments, bent
on control of their people

01:14:13.650 --> 01:14:16.080
and the resources within their borders.

01:14:16.080 --> 01:14:18.630
That willingness to fight
has also been hijacked

01:14:18.630 --> 01:14:21.810
by outside powers, turning
the Kurds into a pawn

01:14:21.810 --> 01:14:24.570
to fulfill geopolitical objectives,

01:14:24.570 --> 01:14:27.360
each time showing how
willing these powers are

01:14:27.360 --> 01:14:30.573
to use the Kurds and
then abandon their cause.

01:14:35.263 --> 01:14:38.057
(tense music)

01:14:38.057 --> 01:14:40.392
(leader speaking in foreign language)

01:14:40.392 --> 01:14:41.940
- [Interviewer] Do the
Palestinians have a right

01:14:41.940 --> 01:14:42.837
to a separate state?

01:14:42.837 --> 01:14:45.890
- [Netanyahu] No, I don't
think they do. But...

01:14:45.890 --> 01:14:49.260
- In 2007, the head of
military intelligence

01:14:49.260 --> 01:14:51.720
for the Israeli army had a meeting

01:14:51.720 --> 01:14:54.420
with the U.S. Ambassador in Tel Aviv.

01:14:54.420 --> 01:14:56.250
We're looking at the classified cable

01:14:56.250 --> 01:14:58.950
that summarizes what was
talked about in this meeting.

01:15:00.570 --> 01:15:03.420
The topic of discussion was Iran, Syria,

01:15:03.420 --> 01:15:05.395
the Gaza Strip, and Hamas.

01:15:05.395 --> 01:15:06.990
(loudspeaker blares)

01:15:06.990 --> 01:15:09.480
Hamas had just won the
Palestinian elections,

01:15:09.480 --> 01:15:12.540
which kicked off a fight with
the other Palestinian group,

01:15:12.540 --> 01:15:16.020
which ended in Hamas taking
over Gaza completely.

01:15:16.020 --> 01:15:16.980
They controlled it.

01:15:16.980 --> 01:15:19.590
And if you're an Israeli
citizen or the U.S. government,

01:15:19.590 --> 01:15:21.720
this is a terrible set of events.

01:15:21.720 --> 01:15:23.880
Hamas is a violent extremist group

01:15:23.880 --> 01:15:25.530
known to commit heinous violence

01:15:25.530 --> 01:15:27.480
against civilians in Israel,

01:15:27.480 --> 01:15:29.010
and they were now in power.

01:15:29.010 --> 01:15:31.770
They controlled the Gaza Strip
an hour away from Tel Aviv.

01:15:31.770 --> 01:15:33.390
But look at this leaked document.

01:15:33.390 --> 01:15:34.470
In this leaked cable,

01:15:34.470 --> 01:15:36.360
you see that the Israeli official says

01:15:36.360 --> 01:15:39.540
that Israel would be happy
if Hamas took over Gaza

01:15:39.540 --> 01:15:41.910
because it would mean that
Israel could now treat Gaza

01:15:41.910 --> 01:15:43.560
like a hostile country.

01:15:43.560 --> 01:15:45.480
- [Reporter] Three days post cease fire,

01:15:45.480 --> 01:15:48.180
and there's unrelenting bombing in Gaza.

01:15:48.180 --> 01:15:50.940
- This document is a view into a strategy

01:15:50.940 --> 01:15:53.340
that right-wing factions
within the Israeli government

01:15:53.340 --> 01:15:55.380
have used for decades in an effort

01:15:55.380 --> 01:15:58.230
to win one of the most divisive conflicts

01:15:58.230 --> 01:15:59.340
in the world today,

01:15:59.340 --> 01:16:03.420
in which two groups are fighting
over one piece of holy land

01:16:03.420 --> 01:16:06.990
and one side is winning by
using a very specific tactic,

01:16:06.990 --> 01:16:09.780
one that the world says
is illegal and immoral,

01:16:09.780 --> 01:16:12.480
and one that worked for a short time,

01:16:12.480 --> 01:16:15.240
but that recently has been shown

01:16:15.240 --> 01:16:17.610
to be a recipe for even worse violence

01:16:17.610 --> 01:16:19.217
and conflict and suffering.

01:16:19.217 --> 01:16:22.050
(serious music)

01:16:22.050 --> 01:16:24.630
In this video, I wanna lay out
what this strategy looks like

01:16:24.630 --> 01:16:25.950
and show you how it failed.

01:16:25.950 --> 01:16:29.040
I know this is a topic that
is full of deep emotions

01:16:29.040 --> 01:16:32.130
that has real stakes in people's lives.

01:16:32.130 --> 01:16:34.980
Please know that I am
earnest in my efforts

01:16:34.980 --> 01:16:37.770
to tell this story with
clarity and with accuracy.

01:16:37.770 --> 01:16:40.440
And also please note that
this is not a full account

01:16:40.440 --> 01:16:43.200
of the conflict between
Israel and its neighbors,

01:16:43.200 --> 01:16:46.680
but I do hope that it sheds
light on a view of the conflict

01:16:46.680 --> 01:16:49.030
that sometimes gets lost
in all of the yelling.

01:16:56.265 --> 01:17:01.015
(Netanyahu speaking in foreign language)

01:17:02.479 --> 01:17:05.229
(crowd cheering)

01:17:11.973 --> 01:17:14.640
(subdued music)

01:17:16.710 --> 01:17:19.800
For 2,000 years, Jewish
people around the world

01:17:19.800 --> 01:17:22.470
have been persecuted and segregated

01:17:22.470 --> 01:17:25.590
and ostracized from society.

01:17:25.590 --> 01:17:26.580
That is a fact.

01:17:26.580 --> 01:17:28.950
By the time the 1800s came around,

01:17:28.950 --> 01:17:31.890
it became clear that
wherever the Jews went,

01:17:31.890 --> 01:17:33.573
persecution would follow.

01:17:39.120 --> 01:17:42.600
This is when a movement
emerged calling for Jews

01:17:42.600 --> 01:17:45.990
to come together and to create
a country for themselves

01:17:45.990 --> 01:17:47.220
where they could govern themselves

01:17:47.220 --> 01:17:50.190
and be free from all
of this racist hatred.

01:17:50.190 --> 01:17:52.050
The creation of a Jewish country

01:17:52.050 --> 01:17:54.540
would have at the top of its priority list

01:17:54.540 --> 01:17:56.490
the security of the Jewish people.

01:17:56.490 --> 01:17:57.720
But the big question was where?

01:17:57.720 --> 01:17:59.760
Several places floated
around in proposals,

01:17:59.760 --> 01:18:02.310
Argentina, even modern-day Kenya,

01:18:02.310 --> 01:18:03.873
which back then was Uganda.

01:18:05.970 --> 01:18:08.790
But most people in this
movement wanted the Jews

01:18:08.790 --> 01:18:11.160
to return to their historic homeland,

01:18:11.160 --> 01:18:14.893
a place called Palestine.
(gentle music)

01:18:16.650 --> 01:18:18.300
Where Jews built their temple

01:18:18.300 --> 01:18:20.730
and their culture 3,000 years ago,

01:18:20.730 --> 01:18:21.900
but then were exiled,

01:18:21.900 --> 01:18:24.420
and now there was this call to return

01:18:24.420 --> 01:18:25.890
so that Jews could feel safe

01:18:25.890 --> 01:18:28.623
after 18 centuries of Jewish suffering.

01:18:31.200 --> 01:18:33.090
So as the 1900s came around,

01:18:33.090 --> 01:18:35.640
tens of thousands of
Jews, mostly from Europe,

01:18:35.640 --> 01:18:37.323
flocked to Palestine,

01:18:39.330 --> 01:18:42.030
which eventually came under
control of the British.

01:18:42.030 --> 01:18:44.400
The British were getting
ready to leave this region

01:18:44.400 --> 01:18:47.280
and were struggling to
contain the growing conflict

01:18:47.280 --> 01:18:50.850
between native Arabs and
all these Jewish immigrants.

01:18:50.850 --> 01:18:54.150
Then in the 1940s came a horrific genocide

01:18:54.150 --> 01:18:56.280
against the Jewish people in Europe,

01:18:56.280 --> 01:18:58.770
led out by Hitler and his Nazi regime.

01:18:58.770 --> 01:19:01.170
This created a wave of
international support

01:19:01.170 --> 01:19:03.810
for this idea of giving the Jewish people

01:19:03.810 --> 01:19:05.790
a homeland where they could be safe.

01:19:05.790 --> 01:19:08.160
Before they left, the British asked the UN

01:19:08.160 --> 01:19:11.130
to determine what would
replace them in Palestine,

01:19:11.130 --> 01:19:12.990
and the UN decided that Palestine

01:19:12.990 --> 01:19:14.640
would become two new countries,

01:19:14.640 --> 01:19:18.030
one for the Jews and one
for the Palestinian Arabs

01:19:18.030 --> 01:19:19.950
that had already been
living in this region.

01:19:19.950 --> 01:19:21.746
- [Reporter] The Jewish
state colored light,

01:19:21.746 --> 01:19:23.362
the Arab state dark.

01:19:23.362 --> 01:19:26.460
Jaffa to go to the Arabs,
Jerusalem internationalized.

01:19:26.460 --> 01:19:30.630
- But as happens when outsiders
draw lines on old land,

01:19:30.630 --> 01:19:31.890
there was a problem here.

01:19:31.890 --> 01:19:32.970
Within these borders

01:19:32.970 --> 01:19:35.340
that were meant for
the new Jewish country,

01:19:35.340 --> 01:19:38.400
hundreds of thousands of
Palestinian Arabs were living

01:19:38.400 --> 01:19:41.070
who would soon have to leave their homes

01:19:41.070 --> 01:19:43.272
to move to their side of the line.

01:19:43.272 --> 01:19:46.855
(gentle distressing music)

01:19:49.320 --> 01:19:50.430
Okay, wait. I'm gonna pause there.

01:19:50.430 --> 01:19:53.070
Because as I said this
is not a full history

01:19:53.070 --> 01:19:54.780
of the Arab-Israeli conflict.

01:19:54.780 --> 01:19:56.010
We actually just made a video

01:19:56.010 --> 01:19:57.630
on our new channel Search Party,

01:19:57.630 --> 01:20:00.480
which focuses on what happens next,

01:20:00.480 --> 01:20:03.300
the conflict between Israel
and its Arab neighbors.

01:20:03.300 --> 01:20:05.130
You can go watch that.
Link's in the description.

01:20:05.130 --> 01:20:06.420
It'll give you some useful context.

01:20:06.420 --> 01:20:09.420
For now just know that this
led to a horrific conflict.

01:20:09.420 --> 01:20:12.270
Jewish militias forced over 700,000 Arabs

01:20:12.270 --> 01:20:14.880
out of their homes turning
them into refugees.

01:20:14.880 --> 01:20:16.890
The proposed borders shifted around,

01:20:16.890 --> 01:20:18.510
turned into ceasefire lines,

01:20:18.510 --> 01:20:20.190
and after all was said and done,

01:20:20.190 --> 01:20:23.490
the Jewish people did indeed
get their own country,

01:20:23.490 --> 01:20:25.650
the state of Israel.
(lofty music)

01:20:25.650 --> 01:20:28.230
And the two important points
here are that number one,

01:20:28.230 --> 01:20:30.960
the very foundation of the Israeli country

01:20:30.960 --> 01:20:32.850
is for security of the Jewish people

01:20:32.850 --> 01:20:35.460
after nearly 2,000 years of persecution.

01:20:35.460 --> 01:20:39.420
And number two, the location
they chose to set it up

01:20:39.420 --> 01:20:41.580
was becoming, as a
result of this conflict,

01:20:41.580 --> 01:20:43.143
not much safer than Europe.

01:20:49.350 --> 01:20:52.138
That's a tension that
follows this whole story.

01:20:52.138 --> 01:20:54.690
(inquisitive music)

01:20:54.690 --> 01:20:57.630
Okay, so now let's fast forward to 1967.

01:20:57.630 --> 01:20:58.740
Israel has its country

01:20:58.740 --> 01:21:01.050
and they fight a short war
with their Arab neighbors,

01:21:01.050 --> 01:21:04.023
and they win that war and they
take over all of this land.

01:21:05.558 --> 01:21:07.080
It's a huge victory for them.

01:21:07.080 --> 01:21:08.970
I'm gonna take away the
Sinai Peninsula from here

01:21:08.970 --> 01:21:10.530
because they did give that back to Egypt

01:21:10.530 --> 01:21:12.690
as part of a peace deal a few years later.

01:21:12.690 --> 01:21:15.390
Israel now controls
important pieces of land

01:21:15.390 --> 01:21:17.373
that enlarge their Jewish country.

01:21:19.950 --> 01:21:23.100
Many saw this victory as a sign from God

01:21:23.100 --> 01:21:25.650
that they were actually
entitled to be here.

01:21:25.650 --> 01:21:27.990
But once again, Palestinians,

01:21:27.990 --> 01:21:30.720
nearly a million of whom had
been kicked out of their homes,

01:21:30.720 --> 01:21:33.450
were living here in the West
Bank and the Gaza Strip,

01:21:33.450 --> 01:21:35.010
which Israel now controlled,

01:21:35.010 --> 01:21:37.110
but they weren't really
sure what to do with it.

01:21:37.110 --> 01:21:39.840
And it's this territory
that would become the stage

01:21:39.840 --> 01:21:42.810
for the strategy that is
the topic of this video,

01:21:42.810 --> 01:21:45.780
where over time this
land would be sliced up

01:21:45.780 --> 01:21:47.730
with roads and checkpoints,

01:21:47.730 --> 01:21:50.010
walls and other military infrastructure

01:21:50.010 --> 01:21:51.840
that would control the movement

01:21:51.840 --> 01:21:53.913
and lives of the Palestinians.

01:21:54.780 --> 01:21:57.900
Soon, even Israeli citizens
would start to move out here

01:21:57.900 --> 01:22:00.870
in large numbers building full-on towns

01:22:00.870 --> 01:22:03.150
and further dividing up this territory.

01:22:03.150 --> 01:22:06.390
Moving citizens into
occupied territory like this

01:22:06.390 --> 01:22:09.543
is something that the world
has deemed illegal and immoral.

01:22:11.070 --> 01:22:13.620
So this occupation starts in 1967

01:22:13.620 --> 01:22:15.480
and it goes on for decades,

01:22:15.480 --> 01:22:18.450
until eventually the
Palestinians living here

01:22:18.450 --> 01:22:20.810
can't handle it anymore and
they start fighting back.

01:22:20.810 --> 01:22:23.477
(intense music)

01:22:24.870 --> 01:22:28.293
This is known as the first
uprising or Intifada.

01:22:30.390 --> 01:22:31.650
It started with boycotts,

01:22:31.650 --> 01:22:34.080
but escalated into mass protests

01:22:34.080 --> 01:22:36.870
where Palestinians of all
ages would throw stones

01:22:36.870 --> 01:22:38.880
and sometimes Molotov cocktails

01:22:38.880 --> 01:22:41.040
at much better-equipped Israeli soldiers.

01:22:41.040 --> 01:22:43.350
It was Palestinian rage exploding

01:22:43.350 --> 01:22:46.770
against Israeli occupation,
and it went on for years.

01:22:46.770 --> 01:22:49.260
The Israeli government would
respond by cracking down,

01:22:49.260 --> 01:22:51.690
killing many Palestinians.

01:22:51.690 --> 01:22:53.820
Another important thing that
happens around the same time

01:22:53.820 --> 01:22:57.090
down in the occupied Gaza Strip
is that a new movement forms

01:22:57.090 --> 01:22:59.790
promising to fight back
against this occupation

01:22:59.790 --> 01:23:01.680
calling for the destruction of Israel.

01:23:01.680 --> 01:23:03.333
The group is called Hamas.

01:23:05.550 --> 01:23:09.030
The first Intifada showed
that this wasn't gonna work.

01:23:09.030 --> 01:23:12.030
Chopping up Palestinian
land, oppressing them,

01:23:12.030 --> 01:23:14.370
keeping them in this occupation,

01:23:14.370 --> 01:23:16.530
was only going to produce more violence.

01:23:16.530 --> 01:23:18.990
It wasn't gonna fulfill Israel's promise

01:23:18.990 --> 01:23:21.930
to provide security and
safety for the Jewish people.

01:23:21.930 --> 01:23:23.221
They had to switch course.

01:23:23.221 --> 01:23:27.270
- The security of the Israeli
people will be reconciled

01:23:27.270 --> 01:23:30.030
with the hopes of the Palestinian people

01:23:30.030 --> 01:23:34.076
and there will be more
security and more hope for all.

01:23:34.076 --> 01:23:35.460
- [Johnny] So in the 1990s,

01:23:35.460 --> 01:23:37.410
they start getting
serious about peace talks

01:23:37.410 --> 01:23:38.243
with the Palestinians,

01:23:38.243 --> 01:23:40.701
and they come to this agreement
called the Oslo Accords,

01:23:40.701 --> 01:23:42.150
(stirring music)

01:23:42.150 --> 01:23:43.800
which for the first time establishes

01:23:43.800 --> 01:23:45.780
a Palestinian government authority

01:23:45.780 --> 01:23:48.240
and giving it power to
govern pockets of land

01:23:48.240 --> 01:23:49.620
in the West Bank.

01:23:49.620 --> 01:23:52.500
It also gave the
Palestinians some authority

01:23:52.500 --> 01:23:54.390
over almost all of the Gaza Strip,

01:23:54.390 --> 01:23:57.340
though there were still
settlements in all of these places.

01:23:59.220 --> 01:24:01.170
This was a big deal for this conflict.

01:24:01.170 --> 01:24:02.640
Like, both sides were
talking to each other

01:24:02.640 --> 01:24:03.660
and coming to agreements

01:24:03.660 --> 01:24:06.450
that was giving, like,
authority to the Palestinians.

01:24:06.450 --> 01:24:08.310
But another theme of the story

01:24:08.310 --> 01:24:11.307
is that hardliners can use
violence to derail peace.

01:24:11.307 --> 01:24:12.937
And that's exactly what happened here.

01:24:12.937 --> 01:24:15.300
(protesters chant)
(brooding music)

01:24:15.300 --> 01:24:17.910
Right-wing Israelis start holding rallies,

01:24:17.910 --> 01:24:20.550
calling their Prime Minister
a traitor and a Nazi

01:24:20.550 --> 01:24:22.620
for giving land to the Palestinians.

01:24:22.620 --> 01:24:23.940
Some of these rallies are led

01:24:23.940 --> 01:24:27.180
by a now familiar character,
Benjamin Netanyahu.

01:24:27.180 --> 01:24:29.880
- The people of Israel want a real peace

01:24:29.880 --> 01:24:31.980
and real peace means peace with security.

01:24:31.980 --> 01:24:34.350
Peace they can trust with
a partner they can trust,

01:24:34.350 --> 01:24:36.030
and they don't feel they have it here.

01:24:36.030 --> 01:24:38.130
We want a real peace, not a fake one.

01:24:38.130 --> 01:24:39.480
- [Johnny] But the peace talks continue.

01:24:39.480 --> 01:24:44.250
- With all our neighbors,
a comprehensive peace.

01:24:44.250 --> 01:24:45.390
- And shortly after signing

01:24:45.390 --> 01:24:48.540
the second part of this deal
to give Palestinians some land,

01:24:48.540 --> 01:24:50.520
the Prime Minister Yitzhak Rabin

01:24:50.520 --> 01:24:52.773
is assassinated by a far-right Israeli.

01:24:53.940 --> 01:24:56.070
Hamas conducts bus bombings.

01:24:56.070 --> 01:24:58.680
And the next year, Benjamin Netanyahu

01:24:58.680 --> 01:25:00.963
is elected as the prime
minister of Israel.

01:25:02.520 --> 01:25:05.190
And Netanyahu is a key
figure in this story

01:25:05.190 --> 01:25:08.970
because his worldview
embodies a way of thinking

01:25:08.970 --> 01:25:11.820
that has taken root in
Israel in recent years.

01:25:11.820 --> 01:25:14.520
The idea that the only
way to give true security

01:25:14.520 --> 01:25:17.160
to the Jewish people is by
doing whatever is necessary

01:25:17.160 --> 01:25:20.550
to stop the Palestinians
from having a state

01:25:20.550 --> 01:25:22.743
anywhere in these borders.

01:25:22.743 --> 01:25:25.326
(gentle music)

01:25:26.910 --> 01:25:28.740
- Look, I'm 28 years old.

01:25:28.740 --> 01:25:30.180
I've had to defend my country

01:25:30.180 --> 01:25:31.710
in two wars and in many battles.

01:25:31.710 --> 01:25:34.290
Nobody wants peace more than Israel.

01:25:34.290 --> 01:25:37.020
But the stumbling block
to the road for peace

01:25:37.020 --> 01:25:40.380
is this demand for a PLO state,
which will mean more war,

01:25:40.380 --> 01:25:42.570
which will mean more
violence in the Middle East.

01:25:42.570 --> 01:25:43.910
And I think, I sincerely believe,

01:25:43.910 --> 01:25:45.720
if this demand is abandoned,

01:25:45.720 --> 01:25:47.460
we can have real and genuine peace.

01:25:47.460 --> 01:25:50.220
- So that was Netanyahu.
He was a 28-year-old.

01:25:50.220 --> 01:25:52.530
But when he becomes the prime minister

01:25:52.530 --> 01:25:53.760
a couple decades later,

01:25:53.760 --> 01:25:57.150
he spends his term
sabotaging the peace accords

01:25:57.150 --> 01:25:59.880
that his predecessor had
worked so hard to create,

01:25:59.880 --> 01:26:02.280
claiming that the
occupation of all this land

01:26:02.280 --> 01:26:05.010
and its people wasn't actually conquest,

01:26:05.010 --> 01:26:08.250
but rather the key for
security of the Jewish people.

01:26:08.250 --> 01:26:09.090
They had to do this.

01:26:09.090 --> 01:26:12.960
Security was the one and only
justification for all of this.

01:26:12.960 --> 01:26:15.000
So under his watch settlers continue

01:26:15.000 --> 01:26:16.623
to move into the West Bank.

01:26:18.840 --> 01:26:22.470
We found this leaked video
of Benjamin Netanyahu

01:26:22.470 --> 01:26:24.407
talking to some settlers in the West Bank.

01:26:24.407 --> 01:26:28.950
(all speaking in foreign language)

01:26:28.950 --> 01:26:31.950
- The cameraman does turn
off the camera for a moment,

01:26:31.950 --> 01:26:34.964
but then turns it back on moments later.

01:26:34.964 --> 01:26:39.464
(Netanyahu speaking foreign language)

01:26:40.530 --> 01:26:44.340
- He is admitting to
sabotaging the peace accords

01:26:44.340 --> 01:26:47.520
that the Israeli government had signed

01:26:47.520 --> 01:26:49.830
with the Palestinians,

01:26:49.830 --> 01:26:51.270
that because he disagreed with them,

01:26:51.270 --> 01:26:52.650
he wanted to sabotage them

01:26:52.650 --> 01:26:55.050
because he was so against
a Palestinian state

01:26:55.050 --> 01:26:58.257
or any form of Palestinian
autonomy in this land.

01:26:58.257 --> 01:27:00.120
And then he goes on to explain

01:27:00.120 --> 01:27:02.962
what his real thinking
is on the situation.

01:27:02.962 --> 01:27:07.462
(Netanyahu speaking foreign language)

01:27:18.000 --> 01:27:21.390
- Netanyahu is a fantastic
politician and statesman,

01:27:21.390 --> 01:27:23.910
and he's able to sort of cover
up a lot of these policies

01:27:23.910 --> 01:27:25.980
in the name of security.

01:27:25.980 --> 01:27:28.530
But here we see what he really thinks

01:27:28.530 --> 01:27:30.690
as he's talking to these settlers

01:27:30.690 --> 01:27:32.040
thinking he's not being recorded.

01:27:32.040 --> 01:27:36.090
So unsurprisingly the
appetite for peace breaks down

01:27:36.090 --> 01:27:37.560
on both sides.

01:27:37.560 --> 01:27:39.060
Palestinians come to the conclusion

01:27:39.060 --> 01:27:41.160
that the Israelis aren't really serious

01:27:41.160 --> 01:27:43.500
about giving them any kind of autonomy

01:27:43.500 --> 01:27:44.610
in the West Bank or Gaza,

01:27:44.610 --> 01:27:46.770
that their situation will never change.

01:27:46.770 --> 01:27:50.370
And once again, they rise
up in a second Intifada.

01:27:50.370 --> 01:27:53.208
This one, much more violent,
much more coordinated.

01:27:53.208 --> 01:27:55.875
(intense music)

01:27:57.450 --> 01:28:00.750
Hamas becomes a major
player in the violence

01:28:00.750 --> 01:28:03.180
with suicide bombings and attacks.

01:28:03.180 --> 01:28:06.223
Israel responds with great
force and during the fighting,

01:28:06.223 --> 01:28:10.170
1,000 Israelis and 3,000
Palestinians are killed.

01:28:10.170 --> 01:28:12.990
At this point the Netanyahu
way of seeing the world

01:28:12.990 --> 01:28:14.850
is starting to look a lot better.

01:28:14.850 --> 01:28:16.080
Peace talks didn't work.

01:28:16.080 --> 01:28:18.060
All they did was produce more violence.

01:28:18.060 --> 01:28:20.730
And so maybe the only
way to ensure security

01:28:20.730 --> 01:28:23.100
is to go back to full-blown occupation

01:28:23.100 --> 01:28:26.100
of controlling every
move of the Palestinians

01:28:26.100 --> 01:28:27.630
in the West Bank and the Gaza Strip.

01:28:27.630 --> 01:28:29.400
So at this point the occupation

01:28:29.400 --> 01:28:30.870
gets more and more suffocating,

01:28:30.870 --> 01:28:32.220
more walls, more barriers,

01:28:32.220 --> 01:28:34.473
more checkpoints, more settlements.

01:28:40.110 --> 01:28:43.350
Then in 2005, Israel
withdraws from the Gaza Strip,

01:28:43.350 --> 01:28:46.230
letting the Palestinian Authority
have total control there.

01:28:46.230 --> 01:28:48.150
They turn their attention entirely

01:28:48.150 --> 01:28:50.640
to their historic homeland
of Judea and Samaria,

01:28:50.640 --> 01:28:52.080
which is the West Bank.

01:28:52.080 --> 01:28:53.640
The next year, an election is held

01:28:53.640 --> 01:28:55.380
in the Palestinian Authorities

01:28:55.380 --> 01:28:57.690
and the winner surprised the world

01:28:57.690 --> 01:29:00.630
and would create a new
chapter for this conflict.

01:29:00.630 --> 01:29:02.700
The winner of these elections was Hamas.

01:29:02.700 --> 01:29:04.440
- [Reporter] This is a
very, very bad result

01:29:04.440 --> 01:29:07.860
for the Palestinians and for Israel.

01:29:07.860 --> 01:29:09.600
- The incumbent Palestinian party

01:29:09.600 --> 01:29:11.100
that had lost the election

01:29:11.100 --> 01:29:13.440
tried to forcibly hold on to power,

01:29:13.440 --> 01:29:15.780
and soon the two Palestinian parties

01:29:15.780 --> 01:29:17.280
were fighting with each other.

01:29:17.280 --> 01:29:18.870
And it results in this split

01:29:18.870 --> 01:29:21.000
between the two Palestinian governments.

01:29:21.000 --> 01:29:22.440
It turns into violence.

01:29:22.440 --> 01:29:23.640
And when the dust settles,

01:29:23.640 --> 01:29:25.440
there's suddenly a bitter divide

01:29:25.440 --> 01:29:27.780
between these two Palestinian groups,

01:29:27.780 --> 01:29:30.343
Hamas completely taking
over the Gaza Strip.

01:29:30.343 --> 01:29:33.510
(subdued music)

01:29:33.510 --> 01:29:35.100
And this gets us back
to our leaked document

01:29:35.100 --> 01:29:36.390
that we started this video with

01:29:36.390 --> 01:29:38.190
where an Israeli official is saying

01:29:38.190 --> 01:29:40.200
that they would actually be happy

01:29:40.200 --> 01:29:42.780
if Hamas took over the Gaza Strip

01:29:42.780 --> 01:29:46.546
because now they can treat
Gaza like a hostile country.

01:29:46.546 --> 01:29:48.658
(harrowing music)

01:29:48.658 --> 01:29:50.100
(explosions boom)

01:29:50.100 --> 01:29:51.390
Now that they're not occupying it,

01:29:51.390 --> 01:29:52.320
they're not responsible

01:29:52.320 --> 01:29:55.290
for the 2 million civilians
who are living there.

01:29:55.290 --> 01:29:56.610
They can impose a blockade

01:29:56.610 --> 01:29:59.610
to control anything coming
in and out of the Gaza Strip,

01:29:59.610 --> 01:30:02.730
people, food, medicine,
money, building supplies.

01:30:02.730 --> 01:30:05.790
But there was another
reason why Israel was happy

01:30:05.790 --> 01:30:08.130
that Hamas now controlled the Gaza Strip.

01:30:08.130 --> 01:30:10.830
The Palestinian government
was now deeply divided,

01:30:10.830 --> 01:30:13.440
Hamas ruling Gaza and
the West Bank being run

01:30:13.440 --> 01:30:15.990
by a more moderate, secular
Palestinian faction.

01:30:15.990 --> 01:30:19.260
And crucially neither considered
the other to be legitimate,

01:30:19.260 --> 01:30:21.180
which weakened their ability to negotiate

01:30:21.180 --> 01:30:24.360
for any kind of state,
for any kind of country,

01:30:24.360 --> 01:30:26.700
especially when Hamas still refused

01:30:26.700 --> 01:30:29.460
to recognize Israel's right to even exist.

01:30:29.460 --> 01:30:31.860
This division played right into the hands

01:30:31.860 --> 01:30:33.003
of the Israeli right.

01:30:38.070 --> 01:30:40.860
And this gets us back
to Benjamin Netanyahu,

01:30:40.860 --> 01:30:43.478
that enemy of the earlier peace talks.

01:30:43.478 --> 01:30:45.480
(brooding music)

01:30:45.480 --> 01:30:48.690
He gets elected once again in 2009,

01:30:48.690 --> 01:30:51.180
declaring himself Mr. Security

01:30:51.180 --> 01:30:54.420
and promising to provide
safety to Israeli citizens

01:30:54.420 --> 01:30:56.730
who are still shaken
from the second Intifada

01:30:56.730 --> 01:30:59.160
and are now worried
that Hamas now controls

01:30:59.160 --> 01:31:00.870
the entirety of the Gaza Strip.

01:31:00.870 --> 01:31:03.420
Netanyahu's playbook
was already made clear.

01:31:03.420 --> 01:31:04.530
He had said it point blank.

01:31:04.530 --> 01:31:06.060
It's what he had been doing for years.

01:31:06.060 --> 01:31:08.550
Sabotaging peace talks that
would give Palestinians

01:31:08.550 --> 01:31:09.990
any kind of authority over this land,

01:31:09.990 --> 01:31:12.180
and continuing to build settlements,

01:31:12.180 --> 01:31:14.760
while continuing in his
words in that leaked tape

01:31:14.760 --> 01:31:18.510
to hit the Palestinians hard
to make it unbearable for them.

01:31:18.510 --> 01:31:21.720
A complete assault on the
Palestinian government.

01:31:21.720 --> 01:31:25.740
Dividing and slowly conquering
the Palestinian people,

01:31:25.740 --> 01:31:28.170
making life hard and desperate for them,

01:31:28.170 --> 01:31:31.320
controlling their lives,
watching their every move.

01:31:31.320 --> 01:31:35.340
And this is where we get to
this paradoxical alignment,

01:31:35.340 --> 01:31:40.290
almost alliance between
Benjamin Netanyahu and Hamas,

01:31:40.290 --> 01:31:41.368
the enemy of Israel.

01:31:41.368 --> 01:31:44.100
(grim music)

01:31:44.100 --> 01:31:47.940
As long as Hamas held
control over the Gaza Strip,

01:31:47.940 --> 01:31:51.150
the Palestinian cause would
remain weak and divided.

01:31:51.150 --> 01:31:53.820
Netanyahu would feel justified in imposing

01:31:53.820 --> 01:31:56.190
this crippling blockade of the Gaza Strip,

01:31:56.190 --> 01:31:58.110
which in turn gave Hamas legitimacy

01:31:58.110 --> 01:31:59.670
among the people of the Gaza Strip,

01:31:59.670 --> 01:32:01.260
showing that their armed struggle

01:32:01.260 --> 01:32:03.630
against Israeli oppression was justified,

01:32:03.630 --> 01:32:05.670
provoking them to launch
rockets into Israel

01:32:05.670 --> 01:32:07.800
to show that they were
actually doing something

01:32:07.800 --> 01:32:09.720
unlike the Palestinian
Authority in the West Bank,

01:32:09.720 --> 01:32:12.150
which in turn bolstered
Netanyahu's narrative

01:32:12.150 --> 01:32:14.310
that the Palestinians
actually don't want peace,

01:32:14.310 --> 01:32:16.110
they want violence and
the destruction of Israel.

01:32:16.110 --> 01:32:17.730
And the only way for security

01:32:17.730 --> 01:32:20.223
is more occupation, more oppression.

01:32:25.680 --> 01:32:28.950
So instead of try to take Hamas out,

01:32:28.950 --> 01:32:31.530
Netanyahu overtly supported them

01:32:31.530 --> 01:32:34.950
by approving huge transfers
of untraceable cash

01:32:34.950 --> 01:32:38.280
literally delivered in
suitcases into the Gaza Strip,

01:32:38.280 --> 01:32:40.680
cash that would inevitably
end up in the hands of Hamas

01:32:40.680 --> 01:32:42.030
to be used against Israel.

01:32:42.030 --> 01:32:44.610
He legitimized Hamas by
negotiating with them,

01:32:44.610 --> 01:32:46.710
releasing a thousand Palestinian prisoners

01:32:46.710 --> 01:32:48.450
in exchange for one Israeli.

01:32:48.450 --> 01:32:51.630
- The Israeli soldier held
captive by Palestinian militants

01:32:51.630 --> 01:32:54.960
for five years is expected
to be freed within days.

01:32:54.960 --> 01:32:58.740
- The more Netanyahu could
keep Hamas in power in Gaza,

01:32:58.740 --> 01:33:00.330
but keep them contained,

01:33:00.330 --> 01:33:03.360
the more he could ensure that
Palestinians remain divided.

01:33:03.360 --> 01:33:05.340
He could keep peace talks
from ever happening,

01:33:05.340 --> 01:33:08.070
which in turn gave him time to continue

01:33:08.070 --> 01:33:11.280
to pursue his expansionist
project in the West Bank.

01:33:11.280 --> 01:33:13.350
And indeed, since 2009,

01:33:13.350 --> 01:33:15.480
when Netanyahu became the Prime Minister,

01:33:15.480 --> 01:33:18.885
the number of settlements in
the West Bank has only gone up.

01:33:18.885 --> 01:33:21.480
(subdued music)

01:33:21.480 --> 01:33:22.560
And if you look at this map,

01:33:22.560 --> 01:33:25.050
you can see how these settlements

01:33:25.050 --> 01:33:27.870
just weave through and carve up this land,

01:33:27.870 --> 01:33:30.000
making it impossible to even fathom

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:31.770
what a Palestinian state could look like,

01:33:31.770 --> 01:33:35.013
which is precisely the
point of the strategy.

01:33:39.793 --> 01:33:41.280
I actually reported out here,

01:33:41.280 --> 01:33:43.440
visiting the settlements
back when I was at Vox.

01:33:43.440 --> 01:33:45.150
I did a series talking to the settlers,

01:33:45.150 --> 01:33:46.740
trying to understand
why they live out there,

01:33:46.740 --> 01:33:48.720
what it's like to live
in these settlements

01:33:48.720 --> 01:33:51.900
that are strangely peaceful and banal

01:33:51.900 --> 01:33:54.360
and just mundane, people
living their lives,

01:33:54.360 --> 01:33:56.880
because they're protected by the army.

01:33:56.880 --> 01:33:58.320
If you want a deeper dive on settlements,

01:33:58.320 --> 01:33:59.850
you can go watch that series.

01:33:59.850 --> 01:34:02.250
But if you're Netanyahu
over the last 16 years,

01:34:02.250 --> 01:34:03.720
you think your plan is working.

01:34:03.720 --> 01:34:06.030
Like, you see all these
settlements going up,

01:34:06.030 --> 01:34:08.040
the international community
can't do anything about it.

01:34:08.040 --> 01:34:09.120
They keep supporting you.

01:34:09.120 --> 01:34:11.670
Every once in a while there's
some flare up in the West Bank

01:34:11.670 --> 01:34:15.300
where Palestinians get into a
fight with Israeli soldiers,

01:34:15.300 --> 01:34:16.860
but it gets contained.

01:34:16.860 --> 01:34:19.680
Every few years Hamas fires some rockets,

01:34:19.680 --> 01:34:22.387
which then gives Israel the
excuse to go, as they put it,

01:34:22.387 --> 01:34:25.980
"cut the grass" by
conducting a short, swift,

01:34:25.980 --> 01:34:29.400
violent military campaign
to keep Hamas at bay.

01:34:29.400 --> 01:34:30.780
And every day that goes by,

01:34:30.780 --> 01:34:32.340
the notion of a Palestinian state

01:34:32.340 --> 01:34:33.987
becomes less and less feasible.

01:34:33.987 --> 01:34:36.690
(subdued music)

01:34:36.690 --> 01:34:39.510
This is one reason why a
far right Israeli lawmaker

01:34:39.510 --> 01:34:41.487
called Hamas "an asset."

01:34:41.487 --> 01:34:43.890
(pundit speaking in foreign language)

01:34:43.890 --> 01:34:46.380
So divide and conquer has
been the name of the game

01:34:46.380 --> 01:34:47.640
in Israel for a long time,

01:34:47.640 --> 01:34:50.610
but especially in the last
16 years under Netanyahu.

01:34:50.610 --> 01:34:54.300
And again, to the people in
charge, they think it's working.

01:34:54.300 --> 01:34:57.870
Maybe this violent status
quo, this equilibrium can hold

01:34:57.870 --> 01:34:59.790
and the far right can get
exactly what they want.

01:34:59.790 --> 01:35:01.320
Security for the Jewish people

01:35:01.320 --> 01:35:03.780
and expansion into all of this land.

01:35:03.780 --> 01:35:07.530
And maybe the occupation will
break the Palestinian spirit

01:35:07.530 --> 01:35:10.080
and they would give up on
their dream of having a state.

01:35:10.080 --> 01:35:11.530
But that's not what happened.

01:35:12.390 --> 01:35:14.730
On October 7th, 2023,

01:35:14.730 --> 01:35:18.720
we saw how wrongheaded this
theory of security was.

01:35:18.720 --> 01:35:20.880
- In an unprecedented surprise attack,

01:35:20.880 --> 01:35:23.010
the militant Hamas rulers of Gaza

01:35:23.010 --> 01:35:27.060
sent dozens of fighters into
Israel by land, sea, and air.

01:35:27.060 --> 01:35:29.250
- This deadly attack launched by Hamas

01:35:29.250 --> 01:35:31.950
showed us that while Netanyahu's strategy

01:35:31.950 --> 01:35:33.960
of divide and conquer might be good

01:35:33.960 --> 01:35:35.490
for taking over more land,

01:35:35.490 --> 01:35:37.500
what it's not good for is making good

01:35:37.500 --> 01:35:40.200
on the original promise of Israel,

01:35:40.200 --> 01:35:43.320
which is ensuring the
security of the Jewish people.

01:35:43.320 --> 01:35:47.654
In fact, his strategy has
produced exactly the opposite.

01:35:47.654 --> 01:35:51.390
(crowd chanting in foreign language)

01:35:51.390 --> 01:35:54.870
Now, the responsibility for
what happened on October 7th

01:35:54.870 --> 01:35:58.290
lies with the people who
committed those acts of terror,

01:35:58.290 --> 01:36:00.540
Hamas fighters and their leaders.

01:36:00.540 --> 01:36:04.020
There is no excuse or
justification for their actions.

01:36:04.020 --> 01:36:06.030
But the point I'm trying
to make with this video

01:36:06.030 --> 01:36:07.650
is that there's also others

01:36:07.650 --> 01:36:09.060
that need to stand accountable here.

01:36:09.060 --> 01:36:11.610
Those who used Hamas as a pawn

01:36:11.610 --> 01:36:14.580
to continue this
divide-and-conquer policy,

01:36:14.580 --> 01:36:16.320
who are now engaged in a campaign

01:36:16.320 --> 01:36:18.840
of mass bloodshed on civilians,

01:36:18.840 --> 01:36:21.030
they deserve to stand accountable as well,

01:36:21.030 --> 01:36:22.680
to the Israeli people

01:36:22.680 --> 01:36:25.110
and to the countries that support Israel.

01:36:25.110 --> 01:36:27.630
I believe in the need
for a Jewish state. I do.

01:36:27.630 --> 01:36:29.580
I think that's a very reasonable proposal

01:36:29.580 --> 01:36:32.760
that Jewish people should feel
safe somewhere in this world.

01:36:32.760 --> 01:36:36.300
And yet what we're looking at isn't it.

01:36:36.300 --> 01:36:37.620
The Israeli project,

01:36:37.620 --> 01:36:40.680
the way that it's been
wielded in its current form,

01:36:40.680 --> 01:36:42.840
produces the exact opposite

01:36:42.840 --> 01:36:44.553
of security for the Jewish people.

01:36:48.003 --> 01:36:49.703
(serious music)
Look at this map.

01:36:51.270 --> 01:36:53.820
This map shows the thousands of attacks

01:36:53.820 --> 01:36:56.160
that have occurred right
here on this border

01:36:56.160 --> 01:36:59.760
just over the past year in
this fight between Israel

01:36:59.760 --> 01:37:03.164
and one of their biggest
regional enemies, Hezbollah.

01:37:03.164 --> 01:37:06.750
(soldiers chanting in foreign language)

01:37:06.750 --> 01:37:09.690
Hezbollah is one of the biggest
armed groups in the world

01:37:09.690 --> 01:37:12.780
that isn't a nation's military.

01:37:12.780 --> 01:37:15.600
They have tens of thousands
of trained soldiers

01:37:15.600 --> 01:37:17.760
and hundreds of thousands
of missiles and rockets

01:37:17.760 --> 01:37:20.613
capable of reaching
targets all across Israel.

01:37:21.510 --> 01:37:22.920
This threat led Israel

01:37:22.920 --> 01:37:26.280
to conduct a massive set of
attacks against Hezbollah.

01:37:26.280 --> 01:37:28.800
- [Reporter] This large explosion was seen

01:37:28.800 --> 01:37:30.210
near Beirut International Airport.

01:37:30.210 --> 01:37:31.043
- [Johnny] In which they killed

01:37:31.043 --> 01:37:33.030
almost all of the group's top leaders

01:37:33.030 --> 01:37:35.460
weakening Hezbollah immensely,

01:37:35.460 --> 01:37:39.480
followed by a full-on
invasion by Israeli troops

01:37:39.480 --> 01:37:41.760
to denigrate this group even further.

01:37:41.760 --> 01:37:43.950
This has been a massive escalation

01:37:43.950 --> 01:37:46.890
that is now spilling over
into this entire region.

01:37:46.890 --> 01:37:48.510
And to understand how we got here,

01:37:48.510 --> 01:37:51.240
you really have to understand
where Hezbollah came from

01:37:51.240 --> 01:37:54.480
and what this group's fierce
40-year struggle tells us

01:37:54.480 --> 01:37:57.000
about how the modern
Middle East came together

01:37:57.000 --> 01:37:58.773
and how it's now coming apart.

01:38:02.275 --> 01:38:04.692
(grim music)

01:38:13.014 --> 01:38:15.030
The story of Hezbollah really starts

01:38:15.030 --> 01:38:17.700
when the vast Ottoman Empire broke apart

01:38:17.700 --> 01:38:19.410
in the early 1900s.

01:38:19.410 --> 01:38:21.960
Europeans came in and
sliced all of this up,

01:38:21.960 --> 01:38:24.960
France taking all of this territory,

01:38:24.960 --> 01:38:26.400
but then they drew a line here

01:38:26.400 --> 01:38:28.680
to carve out this little
mountainous region,

01:38:28.680 --> 01:38:32.100
one that was populated mostly
by Maronite Christians,

01:38:32.100 --> 01:38:34.440
but the border didn't
include just Christians.

01:38:34.440 --> 01:38:37.440
The French made sure to
include this area to the east

01:38:37.440 --> 01:38:39.480
and this area to the south.

01:38:39.480 --> 01:38:43.020
Areas that contained large
populations of Shia Muslims

01:38:43.020 --> 01:38:45.720
who were now forced into this new country

01:38:45.720 --> 01:38:48.120
where they were made a
minority to the Christians

01:38:48.120 --> 01:38:50.460
along with a few other religious groups.

01:38:50.460 --> 01:38:54.240
We're gonna focus a lot down
here on this Shia heartland

01:38:54.240 --> 01:38:55.410
that would eventually become one of

01:38:55.410 --> 01:38:57.857
the most important regions
in the whole Middle East.

01:38:57.857 --> 01:39:00.857
(suspenseful music)

01:39:06.744 --> 01:39:07.753
(subdued music)

01:39:07.753 --> 01:39:11.880
In 1943, Lebanon gains its
independence from France.

01:39:11.880 --> 01:39:14.520
It creates a constitution
meant to balance the power

01:39:14.520 --> 01:39:16.350
between all of these religious groups,

01:39:16.350 --> 01:39:18.000
but that balance wouldn't last.

01:39:18.000 --> 01:39:20.880
Mostly thanks to what
started happening down here

01:39:20.880 --> 01:39:23.280
where another set of
borders were being carved

01:39:23.280 --> 01:39:24.840
into the Middle East.

01:39:24.840 --> 01:39:28.080
The British had controlled
this, but in 1948, they left

01:39:28.080 --> 01:39:30.600
and the UN helped draw these new lines,

01:39:30.600 --> 01:39:34.350
creating a new Israel
and Palestinian state.

01:39:34.350 --> 01:39:38.280
Decades of war forced out
millions of Palestinians,

01:39:38.280 --> 01:39:41.070
many of whom ended up here in Lebanon.

01:39:41.070 --> 01:39:44.190
These Palestinians are
mostly Sunni Muslim,

01:39:44.190 --> 01:39:48.150
so this upsets the carefully
laid power balance in Lebanon

01:39:48.150 --> 01:39:50.730
and further marginalizes the Shia Muslims

01:39:50.730 --> 01:39:52.860
who were fighting for
their place in the country.

01:39:52.860 --> 01:39:57.360
Then in 1971, an armed militia
made up of Palestinians

01:39:57.360 --> 01:39:59.550
called the Palestinian
Liberation Organization

01:39:59.550 --> 01:40:00.810
moves to Lebanon,

01:40:00.810 --> 01:40:02.490
and they turn this whole region,

01:40:02.490 --> 01:40:05.040
which, again, was made up of mostly Shias,

01:40:05.040 --> 01:40:06.870
into their own little mini state.

01:40:06.870 --> 01:40:10.620
You start to see that Lebanon
is descending into division

01:40:10.620 --> 01:40:12.300
between the different militias

01:40:12.300 --> 01:40:14.850
and powers controlling
parts of the country.

01:40:14.850 --> 01:40:16.200
And in the mid '70s,

01:40:16.200 --> 01:40:18.930
it all breaks down into
a full-fledged civil war

01:40:18.930 --> 01:40:22.233
between a dizzying number
of religious factions.

01:40:23.100 --> 01:40:25.680
It's a war that will pull
in much of the Middle East,

01:40:25.680 --> 01:40:26.513
(grim music)

01:40:26.513 --> 01:40:30.030
and it's a war whose most
important region is down here

01:40:30.030 --> 01:40:32.310
in this border zone
between Israel and Lebanon.

01:40:32.310 --> 01:40:35.490
The place that will soon
give rise to Hezbollah.

01:40:35.490 --> 01:40:36.750
Now, let's talk about Syria.

01:40:36.750 --> 01:40:37.890
They're here right next door,

01:40:37.890 --> 01:40:39.207
and they're watching this civil war

01:40:39.207 --> 01:40:40.890
and they decide to invade,

01:40:40.890 --> 01:40:43.740
to prop up the Maronite
Christian ruling class

01:40:43.740 --> 01:40:45.570
who've become Syria allies.

01:40:45.570 --> 01:40:47.700
They want to do this to
prevent the Civil War

01:40:47.700 --> 01:40:49.800
from spilling over into their territory.

01:40:49.800 --> 01:40:52.230
At this point, Syria
also considers annexing

01:40:52.230 --> 01:40:55.560
the entire country of Lebanon,
making it a part of Syria.

01:40:55.560 --> 01:40:57.960
But eventually, the
relationship between Syria

01:40:57.960 --> 01:41:00.900
and Maronite Christians breaks down,

01:41:00.900 --> 01:41:04.410
and Syria continues to occupy
this part of the country.

01:41:04.410 --> 01:41:05.940
Meanwhile, to the south,

01:41:05.940 --> 01:41:09.210
Israel fears that Syria
is growing too powerful.

01:41:09.210 --> 01:41:11.340
It also wants to wipe out the PLO,

01:41:11.340 --> 01:41:14.040
who is attacking them across
the border from Lebanon.

01:41:14.040 --> 01:41:18.360
So in 1978, Israel enters the
fray invading from the south

01:41:18.360 --> 01:41:20.340
and driving deep into the country.

01:41:20.340 --> 01:41:24.150
Israel succeeds in temporarily
suppressing the PLO,

01:41:24.150 --> 01:41:25.260
but in the process,

01:41:25.260 --> 01:41:27.990
it displaces hundreds
of thousands of locals,

01:41:27.990 --> 01:41:29.763
most of them Shia Muslims.

01:41:31.650 --> 01:41:34.740
It eventually withdraws
after a UN resolution.

01:41:34.740 --> 01:41:38.220
But then, in 1982, after more PLO attacks,

01:41:38.220 --> 01:41:39.780
Israel invades again,

01:41:39.780 --> 01:41:42.240
this time pushing all the way to Beirut,

01:41:42.240 --> 01:41:45.123
fighting both the PLO and Syria.

01:41:46.080 --> 01:41:48.880
And this is where the conflict
takes on a new dimension.

01:41:52.665 --> 01:41:55.380
(high-strung music)

01:41:55.380 --> 01:41:58.887
It's 1979 and over in Iran,

01:41:58.887 --> 01:42:02.400
the people have risen up
against the U.S.-backed dictator

01:42:02.400 --> 01:42:06.810
in this Islamic revolution
led by a Shia Muslim cleric

01:42:06.810 --> 01:42:09.840
who wants to spread this
revolution throughout the region.

01:42:09.840 --> 01:42:11.430
He's looking for allies,

01:42:11.430 --> 01:42:14.850
and in 1982, they find their perfect match

01:42:14.850 --> 01:42:16.500
here in southern Lebanon.

01:42:16.500 --> 01:42:18.570
It's a militia that rose

01:42:18.570 --> 01:42:21.930
to defend against outsiders
trampling their heartland.

01:42:21.930 --> 01:42:25.350
It's called the Hezbollah,
which means party of God.

01:42:25.350 --> 01:42:27.120
Iran picked this group in particular

01:42:27.120 --> 01:42:30.630
because it shares its
goals of Islamic Revolution

01:42:30.630 --> 01:42:34.050
and a deep distrust
and disdain for Israel.

01:42:34.050 --> 01:42:35.910
Iran starts providing Hezbollah

01:42:35.910 --> 01:42:39.450
with money, weapons, soldiers,
training, and leadership.

01:42:39.450 --> 01:42:42.150
And in return, Hezbollah proclaims loyalty

01:42:42.150 --> 01:42:45.210
to the Iranian Revolution
and its supreme leader.

01:42:45.210 --> 01:42:47.340
What started as Lebanon's civil war

01:42:47.340 --> 01:42:49.890
is now a regional war that is heating up.

01:42:49.890 --> 01:42:51.870
So the United States enters

01:42:51.870 --> 01:42:54.060
leading an international
peacekeeping mission

01:42:54.060 --> 01:42:55.830
to try to calm these tensions.

01:42:55.830 --> 01:42:58.680
But of course, Hezbollah
and Iran hate this.

01:42:58.680 --> 01:43:01.500
They now have two prime
targets in their backyard,

01:43:01.500 --> 01:43:05.160
Israel, and these Western
powers led by the U.S..

01:43:05.160 --> 01:43:08.970
So in 1983, they launched a
series of terrorist attacks,

01:43:08.970 --> 01:43:10.860
a truck bomb detonated in front of

01:43:10.860 --> 01:43:13.260
a U.S. and French barracks in Beirut

01:43:13.260 --> 01:43:15.153
that kills over 300 people.

01:43:17.280 --> 01:43:20.010
Most of the world blames
not only Hezbollah,

01:43:20.010 --> 01:43:21.960
but also its backer, Iran.

01:43:21.960 --> 01:43:25.110
The fighting continues until 1989

01:43:25.110 --> 01:43:27.090
when the many groups
fighting this civil war

01:43:27.090 --> 01:43:30.210
come to a peace agreement,
one that bans all militias

01:43:30.210 --> 01:43:31.830
and requires them to give their weapons

01:43:31.830 --> 01:43:33.150
back to the government.

01:43:33.150 --> 01:43:34.680
But there's a big catch here.

01:43:34.680 --> 01:43:36.210
Israel still occupies

01:43:36.210 --> 01:43:38.910
what they call this security buffer zone

01:43:38.910 --> 01:43:40.290
in southern Lebanon.

01:43:40.290 --> 01:43:42.570
So the peace agreement makes an exception

01:43:42.570 --> 01:43:46.980
specifically for efforts that
resist the Israeli occupation,

01:43:46.980 --> 01:43:50.400
a.k.a, they allow Hezbollah
to continue to exist,

01:43:50.400 --> 01:43:51.840
turning them into something more

01:43:51.840 --> 01:43:54.600
than just one of these militias
fighting for their group.

01:43:54.600 --> 01:43:56.730
It gives them a kind of official status

01:43:56.730 --> 01:44:00.600
to continue acting as a
defender of southern Lebanon,

01:44:00.600 --> 01:44:03.210
the country's bulwark against Israel.

01:44:03.210 --> 01:44:05.460
They also develop into
more of a political party

01:44:05.460 --> 01:44:08.220
that gains seats in Lebanon's legislature,

01:44:08.220 --> 01:44:10.770
kind of serving as a parallel government

01:44:10.770 --> 01:44:14.433
providing social services in
the areas that it controls.

01:44:15.678 --> 01:44:18.345
(subdued music)

01:44:21.750 --> 01:44:23.820
So let's look at Hezbollah in this moment,

01:44:23.820 --> 01:44:25.080
because they find themselves

01:44:25.080 --> 01:44:28.860
in the middle of shifting
power games in the Middle East,

01:44:28.860 --> 01:44:31.980
balancing their mandate to
defend their Shia heartland,

01:44:31.980 --> 01:44:33.630
which was their founding motivation,

01:44:33.630 --> 01:44:36.630
but also trying to gain
further influence in the region

01:44:36.630 --> 01:44:38.760
while also appeasing the demands

01:44:38.760 --> 01:44:41.730
of their major supporter, Iran.

01:44:41.730 --> 01:44:45.660
In 2005, Lebanon's prime
minister is assassinated,

01:44:45.660 --> 01:44:47.700
and most Lebanese blame Hezbollah,

01:44:47.700 --> 01:44:50.220
along with its other
foreign supporter, Syria,

01:44:50.220 --> 01:44:52.500
Lebanese people rise up in mass protest,

01:44:52.500 --> 01:44:55.410
and Syria eventually withdraws its forces

01:44:55.410 --> 01:44:58.110
that have occupied Lebanon for 28 years.

01:44:58.110 --> 01:44:59.730
Hezbollah is disgraced.

01:44:59.730 --> 01:45:01.290
Its legitimacy is supposed

01:45:01.290 --> 01:45:03.600
to come from resisting foreign meddling,

01:45:03.600 --> 01:45:06.540
and it's becoming clear
that they have become a pawn

01:45:06.540 --> 01:45:10.443
in the geopolitical game of
regional powers, Syria and Iran.

01:45:11.640 --> 01:45:14.370
But the group is able to
turn Syria's withdrawal

01:45:14.370 --> 01:45:16.050
into their advantage.

01:45:16.050 --> 01:45:19.710
The Syrian occupation had
kept Lebanon somewhat stable,

01:45:19.710 --> 01:45:23.190
so as soon as they left, it
creates this power vacuum

01:45:23.190 --> 01:45:25.560
and allows Hezbollah
to take more territory,

01:45:25.560 --> 01:45:28.260
ramping up attacks across
the border against Israel

01:45:28.260 --> 01:45:31.080
and leading to another
brief war with the IDF.

01:45:31.080 --> 01:45:34.200
Hezbollah continues to be
a useful proxy for Iran,

01:45:34.200 --> 01:45:37.383
and Iran continues to
fund them and arm them.

01:45:38.944 --> 01:45:41.850
And by 2011, Iran and Syria pull Hezbollah

01:45:41.850 --> 01:45:45.930
into another unpopular
conflict, Syria's civil war.

01:45:45.930 --> 01:45:48.060
But this hurts Hezbollah's reputation

01:45:48.060 --> 01:45:49.590
because now they're fighting

01:45:49.590 --> 01:45:53.010
on behalf of Syria's
brutal Iran-backed regime.

01:45:53.010 --> 01:45:54.570
These once-liberators

01:45:54.570 --> 01:45:57.270
have turned into foot
soldiers of oppression

01:45:57.270 --> 01:45:58.980
doing the bidding of outsiders.

01:45:58.980 --> 01:46:01.020
But its last source of legitimacy

01:46:01.020 --> 01:46:03.930
continues to be its resistance to Israel,

01:46:03.930 --> 01:46:06.960
something that Lebanon's own
government is too weak to do.

01:46:06.960 --> 01:46:09.693
This remains their source
of legitimacy today.

01:46:10.860 --> 01:46:13.260
So on October 7th, 2023,

01:46:13.260 --> 01:46:16.560
when Hamas and Israel descended
into this most recent war,

01:46:16.560 --> 01:46:17.820
Hezbollah jumped in,

01:46:17.820 --> 01:46:20.580
launching more attacks against
Lebanon's southern border.

01:46:20.580 --> 01:46:23.340
This is meant to support
Hamas in the Gaza Strip

01:46:23.340 --> 01:46:26.583
and to threaten Israel
with a war on two fronts.

01:46:29.220 --> 01:46:31.620
At first, it seemed to be working.

01:46:31.620 --> 01:46:34.140
Tens of thousands of
Israelis have had to evacuate

01:46:34.140 --> 01:46:36.570
the towns and villages in northern Israel.

01:46:36.570 --> 01:46:39.000
So Israel started firing
back across the border,

01:46:39.000 --> 01:46:42.660
forcing 90,000 people in southern
Lebanon from their homes.

01:46:42.660 --> 01:46:45.150
This, in addition to Israeli strikes

01:46:45.150 --> 01:46:48.150
on Iranian proxies and military officials,

01:46:48.150 --> 01:46:52.860
led Iran to fire its first
ever direct strike on Israel,

01:46:52.860 --> 01:46:55.320
trying to deter it from going any further,

01:46:55.320 --> 01:46:56.820
but it didn't work.

01:46:56.820 --> 01:46:59.910
In September of 2024, Israel escalated,

01:46:59.910 --> 01:47:02.580
surprising Hezbollah
with a series of attacks

01:47:02.580 --> 01:47:05.940
that killed a large part of
the group's top leadership,

01:47:05.940 --> 01:47:08.220
including their decades-long leader.

01:47:08.220 --> 01:47:11.370
A few days later, Israel sent
troops across this border

01:47:11.370 --> 01:47:13.770
with the goal of further
weakening Hezbollah,

01:47:13.770 --> 01:47:15.480
trying to make the situation safe

01:47:15.480 --> 01:47:18.690
for Israelis to return home
to the north of the country.

01:47:18.690 --> 01:47:21.090
And now with Hezbollah in shambles,

01:47:21.090 --> 01:47:24.063
its sponsor, Iran, felt compelled to act.

01:47:25.673 --> 01:47:26.712
(missiles exploding)
- Oh, Jesus.

01:47:26.712 --> 01:47:29.760
- [Danna] What we are all
seeing with our own eyes

01:47:29.760 --> 01:47:33.270
is a major attack from Iran.

01:47:33.270 --> 01:47:35.370
- [Reporter] It's a major attack, Danna,

01:47:35.370 --> 01:47:36.870
and it's an escalation.

01:47:36.870 --> 01:47:37.890
It's an escalation...

01:47:37.890 --> 01:47:39.270
- [Johnny] So even if Hezbollah

01:47:39.270 --> 01:47:42.090
eventually begins to rebuild itself,

01:47:42.090 --> 01:47:44.160
it's unclear what role they will play

01:47:44.160 --> 01:47:46.230
in Iran's proxy network.

01:47:46.230 --> 01:47:48.270
But what is clear is that the clash

01:47:48.270 --> 01:47:50.430
between these two Middle East powers

01:47:50.430 --> 01:47:53.460
remains the central force
animating this region

01:47:53.460 --> 01:47:55.710
towards more and more violence.

01:47:55.710 --> 01:47:59.100
And these recent events
show us clearer than ever

01:47:59.100 --> 01:48:02.190
that Hezbollah was just one foot soldier

01:48:02.190 --> 01:48:05.910
in this growing conflict
between these two powers.

